by-reference leftover binding     |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2028:|       | (coercive and strict), named     | criterion 4); `instanceof` across |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2118:below as a named corner with status **restricted** (behaves differently,\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2309:|                     | variadics, named extras and spread  |                  |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2313:| string keys         | named arguments. Here: refused at   | closes in P4     |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2315:|                     | `G-spread-string-keys`; row 65 is   | named`           |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2348:|                     | a named argument is validated at    |                  |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2350:|                     | fixture `:call-unknown-named-later- |                  |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2423:10. (B8.10) Optional absent includes stay refused at publication until the\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2459:| Input shape                 | mixed PHP text (named by `yang.antlr.md`       |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2512:  named-argument timing and readonly state.\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2515:  survive same-table fetches), named-argument validation after the argument's\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2535:error\\\" (round 7); named-argument errors after all arguments (round 7) and\\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:57:|    | Python-named code                  |                                    |\\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:147:its doctrine. The rulings that rest on it are named so that a rejection of the\\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:1176:  environment as `{:import \\\"./x\\\" \\\"T\\\"}`. Resolving named-type references\\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:1274:  chains, `queueMicrotask` interleavings) is a named corpus group, subject to\\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:1445:|       |                                  | shadowing named export; live      |\\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:1533:- `yang.core.uast`: from `yang.python.antlr.uast`,