t/effect-log))))))'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Loading initial Timbre config from: :default\\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\\n:head yang.call/invoke :result [:yin.k/ok :yang.call/not-callable] :effects [#:yang.call{:reason :yang.call/not-callable, :data #:yang.call{:callee 5}}]\\n:head yang.call/invoke-with :result [:yin.k/ok :yang.call/not-callable] :effects [#:yang.call{:reason :yang.call/not-callable, :data #:yang.call{:callee 5}}]\\n:parent yang.call/invoke :result [:yin.k/ok :yang.call/not-callable] :effects [[21] [] #:yang.call{:reason :yang.call/not-callable, :data #:yang.call{:callee callable}}]\\n:parent yang.call/invoke-with :result [:yin.k/ok :yang.call/not-callable] :effects [[21] [] {} #:yang.call{:reason :yang.call/not-callable, :data #:yang.call{:callee callable}}]\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.prompt.md:13:3. **The versioning inventory** (A2): every affected producer, validator, lowering/reconstruction path, derivation verification, publication path, persisted artifact (INCLUDING the per-host prelude publication artifacts and the oracle's checked-in EDN evidence schemas), and mismatch behavior — and which contracts actually change vs which are only read.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793770000000-architect-hardening-3-design.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:7:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"wc -l docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_unexercised.edn docs/agents/known-gaps.md; cat test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md; cat test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_unexercised.edn; rg -n 'yang.clojure|8\\\\\\\\.10|instruction-budget|recorded-portability|mismatch|blocked|failure|exception' docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md docs/agents/known-gaps.md test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     397 docs/design/yin.cic.spec.md\\n     164 test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md\\n     141 test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn\\n       2 test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_unexercised.edn\\n     584 docs/agents/known-gaps.md\\n    1288 total\\n# Slice 9 kernel differential gate: execution evidence correction\\n\\nThe gate on `yang-hardening2` is **blocked**. The architect denied the prior\\n165/165 closure claim because membership in a static dependency closure did\\nnot prove execution of every arity. That claim is withdrawn. The gate retains\\nits final assertion `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))`; missing execution\\nevidence must fail that assertion.\\n\\nThe 106-fixture corpus still has 102 passing agreements, two recorded\\ndeviations, and two recorded upstream failures. The four narrowly recorded\\nexception dispositions remain declared departures, not agreements. No\\nupstream or `src/cljc/` source changes are made. Admission is unchanged:\\n155 bindings (146 admitted, 9 excluded) and 175 candidate function/arities\\n(165 admitted, 10 excluded).\\n\\nRecorded executions now establish **145/165** admitted arities: 39 directly\\nand 106 through named integrations. The other 20, including `parse/1`, remain\\nuncredited. All 20 unsupported credits from the prior 165/165 claim are\\nwithdrawn. Both C lanes record eight `parse/2` calls and zero `parse/1` calls.\\nThe corrected counts and remaining arities are recorded in\\n[`slice9_evidence.edn`](slice9_evidence.edn) and\\n[`slice9_unexercised.edn`](slice9_unexercised.edn). The 20 earlier residual\\nconsumers in [`fixture_closure.edn`](fixture_closure.edn) retain their concrete\\nexpected outcomes; they do not establish closure of the full inventory.\\n\\n## Consumer evidence\\n\\n- `mkenv` preserves a nonempty global environment and creates empty locals.\\n- `beta-red`, `delta-normalize`, and `delta-normalize-local` have explicit\\n  entry fixtures and missing-reference rejections. The local wrapper also\\n  exercises explicit local definitions and their precedence over an ambient\\n  namespace definition.\\n- `install-unfold-implicit!` installs into both isolated upstream atoms on A.\\n  B/C return an updated immutable context, used by both the delta wrapper and\\n  NBE. Both normalizers read the same installed extension. An installed\\n  refusing extension propagates its original error data.\\n- `install-opacity-function` starts from a refusing policy, explicitly installs\\n  the working policy, then enters the original proof dispatcher through\\n  opaque/transparent steps and qed. A duplicate opaque step rejects. A uses\\n  an isolated namespace and host-local Var policy; B/C thread immutable\\n  definition updates through the explicit context.\\n- `install-fundamental-unparsers!` starts from an empty registry, installs the\\n  fundamental product unparser, then unparses nested implications. Dependent\\n  products and atoms remain unchanged. Direct `prod-impl-unparser` fixtures\\n  also verify its `[term false]` refusal result.\\n- `exists-kw?`, `term?`, `pair?`, and `vectorn?` include false results.\\n  `bound-vars` distinguishes a bound occurrence from entirely free variables.\\n  These fixtures preserve upstream behavior, including its shallow term\\n  validator and the use of `vector` rather than `vector?` in utility predicates.\\n- `proper-type?` enters each arity separately. Unknown variables throw;\\n  a well-typed term whose inferred type is not a sort returns false.\\n- `show-deftype` checks definition, axiom, theorem, implicit, and unknown\\n  labels. It depends only on portable record-kind predicates and returns a\\n  string. Host pprint and stdout functions remain excluded.\\n- `safe-get` covers successful lookup, missing keys, stored false, and stored\\n  nil. The latter three all reject upstream. `vremove` removes every match,\\n  preserves a no-match vector, and propagates a predicate's domain exception.\\n\\n`mkenv`, `appify`, and `bound-vars` have no domain rejection in the pinned\\nsource; the fixtures preserve their constructor, empty-input, and empty-set\\nresults instead of manufacturing refusals. A refused product rewrite is\\nidentified by its explicit modification flag, not mistaken for an exception.\\n\\nThe pinned local delta wrapper has a narrower portability scope than its\\ndocstring suggests: `delta-step` drops `local?` when calling `delta-reduction`\\non a reference. Consequently upstream can resolve a global or host namespace\\ndefinition on that path. The global-result fixture preserves this behavior;\\nthe namespace fixture supplies a local definition that shadows the ambient\\none. The guest boundary still requires explicit definitions and has no host\\nnamespace lookup capability. This round does not repair upstream or claim\\nagreement for ambient-only resolution.\\n\\n## Acceptance counting\\n\\nEvery selected guest function body appends `[guest-function arity]` to an\\nexplicit diagnostic stream at entry. Instrumentation covers all arities of\\nthe functions supplied to each fixture, including higher-order calls through\\nregistries and extension closures. Each C lane creates its own stream.\\nAfter the VM halts, the harness reads that stream through its own\\ncursor, preserving the fixture's original outcome and exception payload.\\nA/B remain uninstrumented. Raw ordered call records are retained under\\n`:c-walker :executed-calls` and `:c-semantic :executed-calls` for every completed\\nfixture. The original uninstrumented fixtures used 1,000,000 instructions per\\nlane. The instrumented fixtures have a 2,000,000 instruction bound because\\nbody-entry stream writes add guest instructions. Reading the completed\\ndiagnostic stream is harness work after halt. This is an instrumentation\\nbudget change, not a new performance acceptance claim.\\n\\nPassing direct fixtures contribute only their original function/argument\\ncount, and only with matching body-entry records in both C lanes. Passing\\nnamed integrations contribute only exact arities recorded in both C lanes.\\nStatic dependency membership contributes no credit. Full branch coverage is\\nnot required. Context adapter identities and explicit extra context arguments\\nare recorded in the evidence; each observed guest arity is checked against\\nthat mapping individually, never against all arities of its function.\\n\\nOnly `:pass` fixture rows contribute exercise evidence. Recorded upstream\\nfailures and deviations do not contribute. Any admitted arity without a\\npassing direct or named integration execution path blocks the gate.\\n\\nThe accounting regression first failed against the old implementation: it\\ncredited the deliberately uncalled arity and accepted missing C-lane traces.\\nIt now requires both traces and leaves unused arities uncredited. A second\\nregression replaces the adapted `parse/1` body in memory with an unconditional\\nerror, then runs `:parse-to-normalize-to-type`. A/B and both C lanes still\\npass; both C traces record `parse/2` and no `parse/1`, and the counter leaves\\n`parse/1` uncredited. Every credited path is also checked against the recorded\\nexecutions of its named fixture. See\\n[`slice9_arity_accounting_test.txt`](slice9_arity_accounting_test.txt).\\n\\n## Recorded portability boundaries\\n\\nThe two `:recorded-deviation` rows remain `:elab-after-qed` and\\n`:check-after-qed`. Upstream embeds `clojure.core/meta`, a host function, in\\nexception data; C carries a guest closure. The original outcomes, comparison\\nflags, exact payload guards, and evidence pointers remain intact. Both rows\\nare listed in `:recorded-portability-boundaries` in the summary. Neither is\\nreported as agreement.\\n\\n## Recorded upstream failures\\n\\n`:typing-ascription` still reaches the upstream declaration\\n`type-of-ascribe`, which has no definition. A raises its original unbound-fn\\nexception; B/C retain the explicit branch-local refusal.\\n\\n`:compile-malformed` still passes scalar proof input `[42]`. A/B raise the\\noriginal native sequence exception; C retains its portable sequence refusal.\\n\\nThese two rows have the distinct disposition `:recorded-upstream-failure` and\\nare listed in `:recorded-upstream-failures`. Their original A/B/C records and\\nfalse agreement flags remain available. The disposition checks the exact\\nfixture ID, input call, exception class/message, B outcome, and both completed\\nC outcomes. Changed calls, IDs, or C payloads are tested to refuse the\\ndisposition. Any other execution failure remains a blocker. No upstream fix,\\naccepted-negative claim, or equality projection is introduced for these rows.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nThe accounting tests pass 2 tests and 22 assertions. An independent audit\\nre-derives all 145 retained arities and all 360 credited fixture paths from\\nthe two raw C traces. The four regression suites pass 122 tests and 1,338\\nassertions. Kondo reports zero errors and warnings; cljstyle and\\n`git diff --check` pass. The full oracle runs 26 tests and 1,879 assertions\\nwith exactly one failure and no errors: its retained\\n`(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))` closure assertion. The missing 20 arities\\ntherefore continue to block acceptance. Verification results are recorded in\\n[`slice9_verification.edn`](slice9_verification.edn), with command outputs\\nbeside it.\\n`yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!` explicitly regenerates\\nboth execution evidence and the remaining-arity inventory; normal tests do\\nnot write them. Evidence retains the pinned upstream revision, compiler\\ndigest, runtime, instruction budget, per-fixture outcomes, diagnostic traces,\\ndependency graph, admission inventory, credited paths, and all four recorded\\nexception dispositions.\\n\\nThe append-only correction in [`known-gaps.md`](../../../docs/agents/known-gaps.md)\\nrecords that host Clojure turns a thrown string into `ClassCastException`,\\ncaught by `catch Exception` but not `catch ExceptionInfo`. Portable `try` binds\\nthe error payload without equivalent runtime class handling; this guest/host\\ngap remains declared.\\n\\nExecution scope is both C evaluators on the JVM. This correction does not\\nclaim renewed architect sign-off or Node/Dart verification, and the blocked\\ngate does not authorize program closure or merge.\\n;; GENERATED from exact execution evidence in both C lanes.\\n{[latte-kernel.defenv/axiom? 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.defenv/definition? 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.defenv/qualify-def 2] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 2] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.defenv/registered-definition? 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.nbe/evaluation 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.nbe/instantiate-def 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.norm/beta-reduction 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.norm/beta-step 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.norm/beta-step 2] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.norm/beta-step-args 2] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.norm/delta-step 4] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.norm/delta-step-args 5] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.norm/instantiate-def 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.norm/redex? 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.presyntax/parse 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.presyntax/parse-arrow-term 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.presyntax/parse-defined-term 4] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.presyntax/parse-product-term 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.proof/abstract-local-calls 4] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.proof/abstract-local-def 4] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.proof/elab-declare 7] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.proof/elab-discharge 6] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.proof/elab-discharge-impl 6] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.proof/elab-have 8] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.proof/elab-have-impl 8] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.proof/gen-local-calls 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.proof/ref-uses-in-term 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.proof/update-def-uses 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.proof/update-var-deps 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/alpha-eq? 2] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/alpha-norm 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/alpha-norm- 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/assumptions 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/binderify 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/free-vars 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/mk-fresh 2] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/mk-fresh 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/prod? 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term- 2] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term- 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/rebinder 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/subst- 4] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/term-reduce 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/top-assumption 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.syntax/vars 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.typing/generalize-params 2] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.typing/prepare-argument-subst 6] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.typing/type-of-app 4] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.typing/type-of-args 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.typing/type-of-refdef 5] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.unparser/unregister-unparser! 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.utils/map-with 3] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.utils/vconcat 2] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.utils/vcons 2] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\", [latte-kernel.utils/zip 1] \\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\"}\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:178:`F` not reducing to a Π is Reject (R-APP, `:not-a-function`). `A' ≢ A` is Reject (R-APP, `:argument-mismatch`).\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:191:**Rule R-CHECK.** `E; Γ ⊢ t : T` iff `E; Γ ⊢ t ⇒ T'` and `E; Γ ⊢ T' ≡ T`. The checker never guesses a type for `t` from `T`; there is no bidirectional refinement in v1. Failure of the conversion is Reject (R-CHECK, `:type-mismatch`) and reports both `T'` and `T` in weak head normal form.\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:245:3. Compare heads: `sort` by L-4; `bvar` by index; `const` with the same name by L-4 on levels, then on mismatch unfold either side by C-4 if transparent and retry; `app` spines by head then pairwise arguments by C-9; `lam` and `pi` by domain then body under the extended context; `let` after zeta.\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:270:**Rule O-4 (no host contribution).** Nothing the executing VM does, no primitive result, no effect and no continuation operation contributes a step to §4. If the kernel's execution encounters a host failure, the outcome is a harness failure, reported outside O-1, never a `Reject`.\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:304:**Example D-c.** `theorem bad [] T (lam (sort zero) (lam (bvar 0) (bvar 1)))` into `·`: Reject (R-CHECK, `:type-mismatch`). The body returns `P`, of type `sort zero`, where `bvar 0`, of type `P`, is required.\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:331:3. During a check the configuration is frozen (kernel plan §5). Any VM-level event that would alter it, a registry extension, a primitive redefinition or a store write outside the checker's own state, is a harness failure under O-4.\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:356:Each fixture records the expected pair of outcomes. A mismatch with the recorded pair blocks; a match with Lean is neither required nor expected.\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:377:`Accept` and `Reject` compare as above. A Yin `Unknown` never matches any oracle outcome and blocks a fixture that claims completed checking. A Lean resource exception is recorded as the oracle's `Unknown`, distinct from a Lean type error. A broken driver, translator or crashed process is a harness failure, not a negative fixture.\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:387:| F-5 | R-APP mismatch: `app t (sort (succ zero))` with `t` from §3.5 | Reject (R-APP) |\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:388:| F-6 | R-LET annotation mismatch | Reject (R-LET) |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:18:| `semantic.scan-test` (then `semantic-register.scan-test`) C4 golden mismatch (JVM, Node) | slow tier at 355bd84b | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | closed 2026-10-14: the `[:c4 :py]` scanner golden regenerated mechanically after the other seat's linker relocation | P2 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:24:| `semantic/frame.cljc` (formerly :141; now ~:159) compares a captured frame's free-environment bindings with the task's free-env by host `=`; not NaN-reflexive on JS/Dart (a NaN-valued free binding in a captured/parked/waiting frame would be `:free-env-mismatch` there; same class as the 8f-3 NaN fix) | 8f-3 NaN ruling §5 | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | closed on branch `srvm-frame-nan` (Architect signed off; the commit is the one adding `bindings=` to frame.cljc): guarded slotwise content equality; JVM focused 116 tests / 1380 assertions and quick tier 4007 tests / 249662 assertions green, host-equality mutant 9 failures; [evidence](../collab/yin-vm/1792082835156-engineer-frame-nan.report.md) (Node/Dart lanes assigned to orchestrator) | P3 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:42:| `yin.vm.values` hashes a `Continuation`/`Closure` payload recursively (`values.cljc:99`, `(:continuation owner payload)`), so hashing a deep VM state overflows the JVM stack: `StackOverflowError` in `APersistentVector.hasheq`/`Murmur3.hashUnordered`, reaching `Continuation.hasheq` and `Closure.hasheq`. Surfaces as `yang.python.antlr.safepoint-test/recursion-error-test`, `linked-safepoint-test/linked-recursion-error-test` and two `e2e-test` recursion tests. Verified identical on shiva AND jupiter at 6d6b7e71 (19/141 + 1 error; 10/51 + 1 error; 42/714 + 2 failures), and present at the PARENT commit 3ab1c925 for safepoint-test; environment-sensitive (the same tests are green on the macOS dev machine at 19/144, 10/53, 42/714) `| bound the hash depth or hash a stable identity instead of the payload; needs a stack-size boundary decision `| yin.vm (value hashing) — NOT yang.python; the Python frontend only surfaces it `| found while closing the yang.python link reds (6d6b7e71); the four link-refusal namespaces were fixed, these three were not and are out of the Python seat's scope | P2 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:43:| Refinement of the row above, with the decisive assertion text: the Python recursion guard does not fire before the JVM stack gives out. `yang.python.antlr.e2e-test/recursion-under-real-hooks-test` (e2e_test.clj:819) expects `#:py{:exception {:type \\\"RecursionError\\\", :args [\\\"maximum recursion depth exceeded\\\"]}}` and gets `[:thrown \\\"java.lang.StackOverflowError\\\"]`. Reproduced on jupiter (independent host, no other lane) and shiva at 6d6b7e71; green on the macOS dev machine. The safepoint/linked-safepoint variants surface the same exhaustion inside `Continuation.hasheq` while hashing the state. So the three remaining yang.python slow reds are ONE root: the guest recursion depth the limit allows exceeds what a default JVM thread stack sustains on Linux `| CLOSED 2026-11-02 (6fae7fbe): the JVM default `ThreadStackSize` is 2048 KB on macOS and 1024 KB on Linux, and the guest code runs on a CREATED thread (raising `ulimit -s` to 64 MB does not help; `-J-Xss32m` makes the failing test pass 1/5/0 on jupiter). Run the affected JVM test lanes with an explicit `-Xss` of at least 2 MB, or make the guard measure remaining stack instead of a fixed depth; done — the `:test` alias now carries `:jvm-opts [\\\"-Xss4m\\\"]`, and every JVM lane inherits it `| yin.vm (recursion guard / thread stack) with the yang.python e2e evidence `| refinement found while verifying the link-reds landing (the engineer's macOS-green counts do not reproduce on Linux) | P2 (closed 2026-11-02: all seven namespaces green on Linux) |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:46:| `(compile ...)` under `:yang.python/antlr` returned an EMPTY string on Node/Dart and dumped the whole prelude (24.8M chars, ~15 s) on the JVM — pre-existing (existed under `(lang :yang.python/antlr)`), made reachable via `(lang :python)` by the legacy retirement (5308e7cf) | closed 2026-10-18 at compile-investigation (b8dbeabf + dbe1d14b + fbfb82b6): the JVM dump was the preview lowering against a nil frontend-session (the whole prelude embedded, rendered four times — now lowered :primed); the Node/Dart empty string was the filled-to-EOF token buffer read as the failure point, classifying every no-viable-alternative error :end and parking the line — the listener's offending token now decides (the JVM keeps its lazy-fill branch, its docstring corrected). Evidence: JVM 21 tests/194 assertions/0 failures, Node 21/70/0 (was 3 failures), Dart 4039 all passed (was 2 failures); deepseek gate READY. Follow-up candidate: the contract test is a proxy — add a submitted-content assertion and a host-neutral :incomplete probe test | closed | yang.python seat | found by the M3 round, deliberately not masked | P2 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:47:| the interactive Dart entry (`dart run bin/yin_repl_main.dart`) fails to COMPILE under the current Flutter selection (mise.toml selects Flutter `latest` on beta): a material `Color resolved = switch (...)` API mismatch — pre-existing (the (host) diff touches no UI code; 