 [gate-syntax-variable? 1] [gate-nbe-quotation 1] [gate-nbe-quotation- 2] [gate-syntax-binder? 1] [gate-nbe-evaluation 4] [gate-syntax-binder? 1] [gate-syntax-app? 1] [gate-syntax-variable? 1] [gate-utils-map-with 3] [gate-nbe-quotation- 2] [gate-syntax-binder? 1] [gate-syntax-app? 1] [gate-syntax-ref? 1] [gate-syntax-ascription? 1] [gate-nbe-quotation- 2] [gate-syntax-binder? 1] [gate-syntax-app? 1] [gate-syntax-ref? 1] [gate-syntax-ascription? 1] [gate-syntax-alpha-eq? 2] [gate-syntax-alpha-norm 1] [gate-syntax-alpha-norm- 3] [gate-syntax-variable? 1] [gate-syntax-binder? 1] [gate-syntax-alpha-norm- 3] [gate-syntax-variable? 1] [gate-syntax-alpha-norm- 3] [gate-syntax-variable? 1] [gate-syntax-binder? 1] [gate-syntax-alpha-norm- 3] [gate-syntax-variable? 1] [gate-syntax-alpha-norm- 3] [gate-syntax-variable? 1] [gate-syntax-alpha-norm 1] [gate-syntax-alpha-norm- 3] [gate-syntax-variable? 1] [gate-syntax-binder? 1] [gate-syntax-alpha-norm- 3] [gate-syntax-variable? 1] [gate-syntax-alpha-norm- 3] [gate-syntax-variable? 1]], :lane :semantic}, :recorded-upstream-failure nil, :status :pass, :c-walker {:status :completed, :outcome [:yin.k/ok [:ko {:msg \\\"Theorem type and proof type do not match.\\\", :thm-type (Π [A ✳] A), :proof-type (Π [A ✳] (Π [x A] A))}]], :shape [nil [:vector [[nil :scalar] [nil [:vector [[nil :scalar] [nil {:msg [[nil :scalar] [nil :scalar]], :thm-type [[nil :scalar] [nil [:sequence [[nil :scalar] [nil [:vector [[nil :scalar] [nil :scalar]]]] [nil :scalar]]]]], :proof-type [[nil :scalar] [nil [:sequence [[nil :scalar] [nil [:vector [[nil :scalar] [nil :scalar]]]] [nil [:sequence [[nil :scalar] [nil [:vector [[nil :scalar] [nil :scalar]]]] [nil :scalar]]]]]]]]}]]]]]]], :executed-calls [[kernel-context 3] [gate-proof-check-proof 5] [gate-syntax-assumptions 1] [gate-syntax-top-assumption 1] [gate-syntax-prod? 1] [gate-syntax-top-assumption 1] [gate-syntax-prod? 1] [gate-proof-compile\n... 2240350 bytes omitted ...\nr` consumers. The emitter branches covered are its map and set branches; the vector branch is an order-preservation control. `arity-error-form` is a covered producer, not a second ordering authority.\\n\\n`compile-literal` and `compile-quote` continue to emit constant/quoted collections as literal data. Their maps/sets already use Jing's unordered value encoding; do not turn them into calls. `compile-application`, `compile-dao-stream-apply-call`, `u/app`, lambda bodies, `let`, `do`, and pre-existing UAST operand vectors remain ordered and MUST NOT be sorted, including explicit `(assoc ...)` and `(conj ...)` calls. `u/sexp->uast` treats its non-list collection values as literals and is not a dynamic collection emitter. No universal “sort every assoc/conj application” transform is authorized. Other frontends are outside this implementation round; equivalent unordered-to-ordered emitters discovered elsewhere require their own bounded repair, not silent scope expansion.\\n\\n## RULING 3 — new fix-round bounds and acceptance contract\\n\\ncc4 r2 correctly stopped. Its forbidden-source rule remains true for that completed round. **A NEW compiler-determinism round is authorized by this contract to edit the following surfaces only; this findings session does not implement that round.** Coordinate shared-file ownership against the dispatch base before editing.\\n\\n| File/surface | Permitted change |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` | Collection-emitter normalization, a private content-key helper if needed, and precise docstrings. No unrelated compiler refactor or exception rewrite. |\\n| `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc` | Only `clojure-manifest`'s compiler revision/lowering-profile declaration and associated description, per RULING 4. |\\n| `test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc` (new) | Portable regression/property and evaluation-order tests below. |\\n| `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` | Preserve/import cc4's strengthened cohort; add focused regression assertions and replace active expectations only through the controlled re-pin below. |\\n| `test/yang/clojure_test.clj`, `test/yang/frontend_test.cljc`, `test/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc` | Focused collection regressions or manifest-revision expectations only where affected. |\\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/` | Versioned post-fix captures/expectations and historical copies needed to retain pre-fix evidence. |\\n| `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` | Manifest inclusion for the changed/new test namespaces only. The four unrelated missing namespaces remain a J2-owner dependency; no exclusions or bypasses. |\\n| New files under `collab/yang-clojure/` | Fix findings, raw evidence, source/toolchain pins, before/after digest ledger, and budget continuation records. |\\n\\nAll other implementation files remain out of bounds: in particular Jing/CBOR, VM grammar and evaluators, `macro.cljc`, semantic lowering/derivers, encoder/loader machinery, shared core prelude, `dht.cljc`, and `slice9_site_tables.edn`. Do not repair this by changing hashing, C1 validation, origin formation, or the oracle. A needed change outside these bounds must be reported as a dependency rather than included incidentally.\\n\\n**Required tests (red before fix; all four hosts use the same recorded expectations):**\\n\\n1. **The reproduced arity-map regression.** Use the existing `argument-vector` and `lower-unit` replay members with their original source, options, and supplied coordinates. Assert the constructor row has the same ordered child-address vector on JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt; its paired operands obey RULING 1. Assert identical whole-tree canonical bytes/root, complete sorted occurrence-key vector, complete C1 relation, and each format's reconstructed instruction-provenance relation. Exercise named and anonymous arity errors, including anonymous source metadata, and verify the resulting arity payload values. The existing reproduced named case is the mandatory red; no special-case producer fix satisfies this test family.\\n2. **Map representation/permutation property.** For a recorded corpus of distinct source-entry pairs, construct extensionally identical maps using insertion permutations and available ordinary array-map/hash-map representations. For sizes 0–4 enumerate all permutations; include sizes 8, 9, 16, and 32 with recorded forward, reverse, rotated, and fixed shuffled permutations so representation thresholds are crossed. Include constant keys/dynamic values, dynamic keys, heterogeneous scalar and quoted collection keys, nested maps/sets/vectors, floats, generated destructuring names, duplicate subtrees, and reader/non-reader metadata. At least one dynamic expression must reach the emitter in each nonconstant case. For fixed options and admission/expansion inputs, every permutation/representation on every host MUST yield identical canonical tree bytes/root, full C1/key vectors, and per-format provenance. Compare byte content, not host array identity or printed forms. Constant cases separately assert the literal fast path.\\n3. **Set representation/permutation property.** The same bounded sizes/permutations for dynamic sets; require identical roots and full relations under a fixed replay. Include nested dynamic sets and different expressions evaluating to the same value. Assert element-address ordering and retain all expression occurrences before runtime set insertion. Do not deduplicate compiled elements as an optimization.\\n4. **Order, pairing, and multiplicity oracle.** Independently project each compiled key/value child and assert that the actual emitted pair-key vector is sorted by the specified comparator, that pairs remain intact, and that the seed is first. Add different source key forms that compile to the same key code with different values to exercise the value-root secondary key; add distinct forms compiling to an identical entire pair/element to exercise ties without occurrence loss. Changing only source-position or variable-node metadata MUST NOT change code order/root. Preserve semantic metadata in literal payloads. Use an independent expectation builder, not the emitter helper being tested.\\n5. **Executable behavior.** Run portable fixtures through walker, semantic, stack, and register execution where those existing routes support them, on the four host lanes. Record an observable trace using the existing test harness's explicit effects/streams: key-before-value, canonical pair/element order, no duplication, and no later event after an operand failure/continuation transfer. Include dynamic keys colliding at runtime and assert the canonically last value wins; include set-value collisions. Compare pure distinct-key results with the unchanged mathematical map/set contents. Explicit `assoc`/`conj` calls, dynamic vectors, `let`, and `do` MUST retain written order; swapping their effectful arguments MUST remain observable and their ordered canonical rows MUST remain distinct. These controls prevent an invalid global sorter from passing.\\n6. **Entry points and generation.** Cover `compile-form`, `compile`, both relevant `compile-program` modes, and `lower-unit`. Keep the real production macro/twin-call fixture and the complete expansion-record chain in the equality gate. Prove that pre-expansion collection normalization does not fabricate or erase expansion origins. Include compiler-generated arity maps rather than testing only hand-built user maps.\\n7. **Legacy loading and identity boundaries.** Load a retained pre-fix artifact by its old address and execute it without recompilation; retain its old C1/provenance if present. Also retain the unannotated legacy-load/missing-C1-refusal tests. Replaying fixed coordinates on the new compiler must agree across hosts; admitting the same content with two different tokens must still produce different origins and occurrence keys.\\n\\nRecord portable generators/permutations as data or use an explicitly specified deterministic generator with recorded seeds; host `rand`, host hash iteration, and test-time self-generated goldens are not an oracle. Any unsupported host/form route must have its exact existing refusal recorded. A newly missing required portable comparison is a failed/incomplete gate, not a green skip.\\n\\n**Regression gate:** re-run cc4's ENTIRE strengthened `yang.clojure-callsite-test` battery on JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt, preserving the eight-member cohort, publications, negative admissions, retained-evidence negatives, and existing honest reader/interop gates. Use the r2 command forms, plus the new collection suite:\\n\\n```text\\nclojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test\\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test --config-merge '{:ns-regexp \\\"^yang\\\\\\\\.clojure-callsite-test$\\\"}'\\nbb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yang.clojure-callsite-test\\nbb src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj core --only '^yang.clojure-callsite-test$'\\n```\\n\\nRun the new portable namespace through the corresponding four selectors as well; run affected compiler/manifest tests and kondo on touched files. Record exact commands, toolchains, source/test pins, executed counts, and refusal inventories. r2's 45 JVM / 40 Node-Dart test counts are historical baselines, not counts to force after adding tests. J2's four-namespace manifest refusal MUST be resolved by its owner before four-host acceptance; zero Jolt children is not a pass. Observe the repository's targeted-test/remote-lane rules and required `dao.stream` merge gate; do not launch a branch full suite as part of this ruling.\\n\\n**Re-pinning is REQUIRED.** This repair changes canonical executable bytes. After reviewing the new operand vectors and establishing raw four-host agreement, record one post-fix reference bundle and use that identical bundle as fixed expectations on every host. Re-record the complete cohort, including unchanged members, so root, full C1/key digests, per-format provenance, producing logs, publication/table/record/manifest addresses, and compiler revision pins remain mutually consistent. No Dart-specific expectation, no runtime recomputation of expected digests, and no origin/path/name normalization are permitted.\\n\\nKeep the r2 divergence file, raw logs, and findings immutable as historical defect evidence. Archive the original active snapshots/captures under an explicitly pre-fix name before replacing any active fixture; publish a before/after ledger keyed by compiler revision and input pins. Re-pinning a failing host in isolation is not a repair. A JVM address changing too is expected and is not grounds to preserve the old broken ordering.\\n\\nThe fix's regression result does not itself close cc4 adoption. Resume cc4's declared B/S, pre/post-port and cross-check-host budget work only after determinism gates pass. Preserve the existing finite ceiling declaration; record any exceedance honestly. Pin this ordering fix separately from Phase 2 `d60038ef`, so its additional compile-time content projection/sorting costs and changed artifact sizes are visible confounders rather than falsely attributed to the continuation port. The r2 report states those measurements were not executed. D1 remains dissolved under the dispatch; this ruling does not revive it.\\n\\n## RULING 4 — versioning, addresses, and legacy artifacts\\n\\n**Yes: there is a one-time canonical shift for affected newly compiled artifacts under this new compiler revision.** Changed collection applications change ancestor roots and may change occurrence paths, C1 keys/tables, instruction vectors/provenance, macro input/output records, and containing publication addresses. Even an application elsewhere in a changed root gets a different C1 key because the root is part of that key. There is no requirement that every artifact changes.\\n\\n**MUST:** advance the Clojure frontend manifest revision from the inspected `\\\"c1-1\\\"` to `\\\"c1-2\\\"` and declare its lowering profile as `:yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1` (if the dispatch base has already advanced, choose and record a fresh nonconflicting successor before recording expectations). Keep the C1 marker value `1` and the existing C1 support claim: identity/coverage schema has not changed. Keep SPI and UAST/execution grammar versions unchanged. The shared UAST-to-instruction lowerer has not changed for a given UAST, so its own lowering-profile stamp must not be bumped merely because this frontend now supplies different input trees. Pin the compiler commit and this frontend ordering profile with the replay fixtures.\\n\\nThis follows the original design's §3.1 distinction between frontend/lowering revisions and execution grammar revisions, and `docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` §5.2.1–5.2.2: content integrity, derivation verification under an exact profile, and executable loadability are distinct obligations. The existing manifest function is at `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:43–54`.\\n\\n**Legacy artifacts MUST continue to load at their original addresses**, subject to their already-existing content/contract/dependency checks. Loaders must not sort their operands, rehash them under the new policy, rewrite stored facts, or relabel old C1 keys as new ones. Old executable operand order remains old executable behavior. No storage rewrite or destructive migration is required. Recompilation/republishing creates new immutable artifacts and new addresses; consumers electing to upgrade update their references explicitly. Old side tables remain attached to old roots, and absent legacy provenance is not fabricated.\\n\\n**Address guarantee:** identical canonical bytes retain identical content addresses regardless of compiler version. Identical source text does NOT promise identical compiled addresses across unpinned compiler/profile revisions. C1 §5.2 replay equality already pins the compiler/profile revision and all other listed inputs; it never guaranteed source-to-address stability across compiler upgrades. Reproducing an old compilation requires its old pinned compiler/profile (or loading its retained output), not silently applying this new normalization. Historical evidence remains valid evidence of its own artifacts, not a certificate for newly compiled roots.\\n\\nAcceptance remains pending the new fix, independently checked re-pins, four-host regression results, legacy execution evidence, and the separate cc4 budget closure. This document rules policy and bounds; it does not claim those gates have passed.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795101450000-architect-fixorder-signoff.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:24:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1795017484194-engineer-cc4-r2-findings.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Created-GMT: 2026-11-18 15:58:04 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-18 22:58:04 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\nCoding-Agent: codex\\nSession-ID: 01a1ea51-a87d-7062-ae12-e6c1c169b48c\\nRole: VM Engineer (compiler provenance)\\nImplementers:\\n- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Status: stopped on compiler divergence | Rationale: same-session r2 continuation\\n\\n# cc4 r2 — STOPPED on reproduced Dart replay divergence\\n\\nRole: VM Engineer (compiler provenance)\\nWorktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc4`\\nBranch/base: `cc4-fourhost-equality` / `2687ab0cf03ebaa232be49a2333347d12a71d9a3`.\\nNo commits. No compiler/source implementation changed. The r1 findings remain\\nunchanged. This report and evidence are written in the authorized worktree;\\nthe orchestrator can mirror them to its checkout.\\n\\n## Verdict and required next round\\n\\n**FAIL: four-host replay equality.** Dart produces different canonical code\\nfor the argument-vector and lower-unit cohort members; C1 keys and instruction\\nprovenance therefore also differ. The focused failing test reproduces this.\\nPer the brief's binding STOP rule, cc4 does not fix the compiler, re-pin Dart,\\nnormalize generated code, or continue budget/acceptance execution after this\\nfailure. A compiler determinism repair needs a separately authorized round.\\nThe acceptance bundle remains blocked. D1 is dissolved per the owner's dispatch;\\nno durable-correspondence verification or D1 consumption is claimed.\\n\\nA second, independent blocker is J2's inherited manifest: four existing test\\nnamespaces are unlisted. The cc4 callsite inclusion is implemented, but the\\nlane refuses before launching a Jolt child. This is a failed required gate,\\nnot an accepted reader limitation or a green skip.\\n\\n## Concrete compiler defect and diverging artifacts\\n\\nAll eight inputs are the SAME `.cljc` source/form literals and options. The\\nsource fixtures include float `1.5`, `^:replay` metadata, destructuring-generated\\ntemporaries, repeated `(identity a)` subtrees, a macro constructing a twin call,\\nwrapper/library/prelude surfaces, and separate supplied admission tokens.\\nNo host-specific source conditional occurs in the cohort itself.\\n\\n| Entry | Application occurrences | JVM and Node canonical root | Dart canonical root |\\n|---|---:|---|---|\\n| argument-vector | 263 on both | `:segment/blake3-a0f9c217122ce675d1b3cd5f899740d604ec35f801eac9a4960153cbcd91d699` | `:segment/blake3-02eac587af541bc180db4109b3accd5e3981a92eb5d1d00e63d6f12d74b484b0` |\\n| lower-unit | 256 on both | `:segment/blake3-44c06492b31348905205b1e1130c27aa1c769790010291ca223d3ab61bfa2775` | `:segment/blake3-9fe835e99e3afc3c2dc7639e7f26d1bcb8ab08445ded6b08aa8d3c78d01546fa` |\\n\\nFor argument-vector, the JVM C1 digest is\\n`82385d11b83bd1a6bd540cc80011ec88f23cf2e9a959fecfd604eff029a1ba2a`, Dart is\\n`a7f9b710743fa0572fc24817d41abfdab16f14ddeef266d31e783fc9dcc59c69`.\\nFor lower-unit, JVM is\\n`654c6a31726250f58550db88ce905fda869f3040b350e298da0aa73995b581ed`, Dart is\\n`73663cae54144b2ea36899e0f134fda95004a66e47812f44a517309a21970514`.\\nFull key-vector and instruction-provenance digests, expected/actual, are retained\\nin `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-dart-divergences.edn`.\\n\\nRead-only comparison of the saved row maps isolates a bottommost difference:\\n`assoc` constructing the generated arity error map. Its arguments are:\\n\\n- JVM/Node: `{} :yin.vm.data/reason :arity :yin.k/argc (data/count dsg__av) :yin.k/fn 'replay`\\n- Dart: `{} :yin.vm.data/reason :arity :yin.k/fn 'replay :yin.k/argc (data/count dsg__av)`\\n\\nThe common operator row is `:variable assoc`. All seven child addresses exist\\nunchanged on both hosts; only the order of the final two key/value pairs differs.\\nThe resulting application addresses are respectively\\n`:segment/blake3-8598820bee9b622d827c7879729f60dad19244f9f9869ee693c1eaca58c1bb94`\\nand\\n`:segment/blake3-9a8f3a641f0e49b7381eccc74a1373b0d6bf97e954964587a449fcc2ee177e9b`.\\nArgument-vector has 494 unique rows on each host, 32 exclusive rows on each;\\nlower-unit has 499 each, 45 exclusive rows on each.\\n\\nLikely cause (inference from saved rows and read-only source inspection):\\n`arity-error-form` at `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1087` constructs a map with\\n`cond->`/`assoc`; `compile-constructed-collection` at `:302–323` emits\\n`(interleave (keys form) (vals form))` without a stable ordering rule. The map's\\nhost iteration order therefore enters canonical application operands. No fix\\nwas attempted; choosing the ordering/evaluation policy is outside cc4.\\nThe runtime meaning may be equivalent for this error map, but C1 replay requires\\nidentical code addresses, and this gate correctly fails it.\\n\\n## Pinned cohort and artifact checklist\\n\\n`replay-expectations` is literal recorded JVM data, not generated expectations\\non each host. `replay-snapshot` hashes the **entire** canonical-byte-sorted\\noccurrence-key vector and C1 relation using Jing BLAKE3; it also pins all three\\nformats' reconstructed call-provenance together. There is no origin/name/path\\nnormalization. The macro entry additionally pins its entire producing log.\\n`jing/canonical-compare` supplies ordering, avoiding host printer order.\\nThe original r1 pin keeps a directly asserted complete eight-key vector too.\\n\\n| Producer / artifact | Pinned surfaces | A | Equality result |\\n|---|---|---:|---|\\n| native `compile-program` | root, full C1/keys, semantic/stack/register provenance | 14 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\\n| `compile-program` with `true yang/unit-opts` | same, including generated arity helper | 263 | JVM/Node match; Dart diverges |\\n| `lower-unit` | wrappers + bundled `library-for`, all C1/keys/provenance | 256 | JVM/Node match; Dart diverges |\\n| `clj-prelude/module-uast` | root and complete static relations | 114 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\\n| production macro expansion | constructed/retained twin origins, full producing log | 5 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\\n| second supplied admission token | same native root, different full origins/keys | 14 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\\n| fresh `yang.call` publication | root, full C1/keys, table/provenance/record/manifest addresses | 100 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\\n| fresh `clj` publication | same complete side artifacts and dependency address | 114 | JVM/Node/Dart match |\\n\\nTotal A = 880, including duplicate admissions and shared prelude content.\\nThis is an occurrence count, not a storage-deduplicated count. The negative fixture\\nuses supplied `\\\"admission-a\\\"` and `\\\"admission-b\\\"` on `:cc4/replay`, member 0;\\nroots match and origin sets differ. Macro coordinates are supplied by the existing\\nproduction-style helper: seed token/medium `:callsite-test/standard-forms`,\\nprogram token `\\\"callsite-test\\\"`, medium `:program-in`, initial t=0. Expansion\\nrecords and their producing chain are included verbatim in the log digest.\\nPublication uses the publisher's recorded deterministic default specification\\nadmission; its real origins are included in the complete C1/key digests.\\n`:origin` is omitted only from the redundant address-summary map, because its\\nprinted keyword is not EDN-reader-safe; no persisted origin is changed.\\n\\nNative uses default opts; the argument-vector and linked unit use the dispatch\\nrevision's `yang/unit-opts`: convention `:arg-vector`, `:outcomes true`,\\n`:linked-runtime true`, `library-adapters`, and `vm/primitive-profiles`.\\nThose historical option names remain as implemented after the continuation port.\\nThe compiler and test file SHA-256 pins below fix all profile/naming inputs.\\n\\nRecorded artifacts:\\n\\n- `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-snapshots.edn`: readable JVM digest/address expectations, matching the literal test data.\\n- `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-jvm.cbor`: the full eight-member JVM trees, C1 relations, sorted key vectors, expansion log, publication payloads and provenance. Binary canonical CBOR retains even origins whose printed keyword cannot be re-read as EDN.\\n- `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-jvm-affected.edn`: complete JVM trees/C1/sorted keys for the two affected members.\\n- `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-dart-divergences.edn`: expected/actual digest snapshots and complete actual Dart trees/C1 rows for those same members.\\n- `collab/yang-clojure/1795017275897-cc4-r2-evidence/`: immutable raw test/refusal logs, JVM capture recipe and row-difference evidence. The focused Dart failure prints the actual producer artifacts before failing.\\n\\n## Host matrix: exact commands and counts\\n\\nAll executed runtime gates here ran on Darwin 25.6.0 arm64, host `darkstar`.\\nTool selection: `export PATH=\\\"$HOME/.local/share/mise/shims:$PATH\\\"`.\\nOpenJDK 21.0.2+13-58; Clojure CLI 1.12.4.1602; Node v25.6.1;\\nFlutter 3.47.8. JVM tests use the repository's `-Xss64m` policy.\\nANTLR prerequisite: `bb gen:antlr` — input/output verified cache hit.\\nSingle-namespace G0 runs comply with the laptop exception; no subsystem/full\\nlane set was launched locally.\\n\\n| Runtime | Command | Result |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| JVM battery | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 45 tests, 597 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\\n| JVM final diagnostic/source verification | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test -v yang.clojure-callsite-test/portable-replay-cohort-test` | 1 test, 11 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\\n| Node initial and final | `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test --config-merge '{:ns-regexp \\\"^yang\\\\\\\\.clojure-callsite-test$\\\"}'` | 40 tests, 508 assertions, 0 failures/errors; all eight snapshots match |\\n| Dart battery | `bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 40 registered tests: 39 pass, 1 fails (cohort); Flutter does not report an assertion tally |\\n| Dart isolated reproduction | `bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yang.clojure-callsite-test/portable-replay-cohort-test` | 1 registered test, fails reproducibly; actual artifacts captured |\\n| Jolt/J2 | `bb src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj core --only '^yang.clojure-callsite-test$'` | exit 1 at manifest; 0 Jolt child tests executed, no digests produced |\\n\\nThe JVM battery preceded the additional diagnostic-only artifact fields and B/S\\npreparation arity; the final focused JVM check and final Node battery include\\nthose changes. The isolated Dart reproduction includes the diagnostic capture.\\nThe original Dart attempt was a toolchain sandbox refusal (Flutter SDK cache\\nwrites denied), not a test result. The retry with cache access compiled and ran,\\nand then exposed the real divergence. No full-suite claim is made.\\n\\nTDD evidence: the initial empty snapshot expectation fails on JVM (1 failed\\nassertion out of 11); subsequent recorded expectations pass. Adding per-format\\nprovenance caused another empty-expectation red before the final recording.\\nThe J2 inclusion assertion initially fails because cc4 is absent; inclusion is\\nnow present in `included` and in `check-manifest!`'s bare inventory. The four\\nother namespace omissions are independently reproduced using HEAD's original\\n`included` and original `check-manifest!` definitions (saved baseline script).\\n\\n## Legacy behavior and refusal inventory\\n\\nThe existing battery passed `published-instruction-provenance-test` on JVM,\\nNode and Dart: an unannotated legacy module publishes with an address and no\\ninstruction-provenance record. `unclaimed-batch-test` and\\n`unclaimed-after-claimed-test` preserve absence of a C1 claim. These are the\\nexisting publication/load boundaries exercised by this battery; no new D1 or\\nuniversal migration claim is inferred from them.\\n\\nThe existing five JVM-only deftest families remain reader-gated on Node/Dart:\\n`repl-packet-provenance-survives-failure-test`,\\n`repl-packet-provenance-survives-link-resume-failure-test`,\\n`repl-packet-provenance-durable-test`,\\n`repl-fabricated-retention-evidence-is-ignored-on-pending-completion-test`, and\\n`repl-fabricated-retention-evidence-is-ignored-from-late-formatting-on-pending-completion-test`.\\nTheir `:cljd nil` and JVM interop restrictions remain intact. Additionally,\\n`repl-query-link-forwarding-test` is registered on Dart but its `with-redefs`\\nspy body is explicitly `:cljd nil`; its green registration is **not evidence\\nthat the forwarding spy executed on Dart**. This is the documented refusal.\\n\\nJ2's global applicability refusal names existing unlisted suites:\\n`yin.repl.php-parser-test`, `yin.vm.code-entry-test`,\\n`yin.vm.machine-data-test`, `yin.vm.provenance-test`. No exclusions were added,\\nremoved or relaxed. The gate's manifest owner needs to reconcile these before\\nJolt can execute cc4. The optional namespace selector cannot bypass this check.\\n\\nThe battery's invalid versions, missing/ambiguous origins, incomplete coverage,\\nwrapper-provenance tampering, fabricated retention evidence, and missing-record\\nnegative cases remain tested under their existing applicability gates. The newly\\nobserved Dart divergence is a compiler defect, not an accepted host refusal.\\n\\n## Budget declaration and stop status\\n\\n`1795016601236-cc4-r2-budget-declaration-v1.md` was written **before budget\\nmeasurements**. It declares finite input, storage, retained heap, peak heap/RSS,\\ncold/warm pipeline, stage and S−B ceilings, derived by scaling cc3 v2's reference\\nceilings with explicit headroom. These are declarations, not measured passes.\\nThe unexecuted preparation harness is preserved as\\n`1795017203479-cc4-r2-budget-runner.cljc.draft`; it is not a validated runner and\\nis deliberately outside test discovery. Its B/S preparation arity is retained\\nin the cohort helper for a later authorized budget round.\\n\\n| Required experiment | Storage | Retained/peak | Pipeline | Verdict |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| pre-port B and S, JVM | not run | not run | not run | blocked by mandatory STOP |\\n| post-port B and S, JVM | not run | not run | not run | blocked by mandatory STOP |\\n| cross-check host B and S | not run | not run | not run | blocked by mandatory STOP |\\n| remaining runtime measurements | not run | not run | not run | blocked by mandatory STOP |\\n| S−B and pre/post shifts | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable | no compliance/attribution result |\\n\\nThe correct pre-port pin is merge `309fe842`'s first parent:\\n`8afd82f5e99d0f2b2d38a5f53b292105fdead688`. The historical depth table's\\n`fbd8da0f` baseline is not substituted for this required pin. A source-only\\nhistorical copy and a minimal common corpus were prepared under ignored\\n`target/cc4-preport` and `target/cc4-postport`; **no budget run was launched**.\\nFuture measured pre/post shifts must be attributed to Phase 2 `d60038ef`, with\\nother intervening base changes documented as confounders. The declaration\\nstates the B limitation explicitly: compiling annotations is common work, so\\nstripping them before downstream B operations only isolates downstream S−B.\\nNo zero compile overhead, measured memory, budget pass or failed bound is claimed.\\n\\n## Remote approval review and scope\\n\\nRead-only load checks reached both designated hosts, both idle relative to core\\ncount; no Dart lane was running. A request to create\\n`~/ci/datomworld-cc4-r2-node` on jupiter from the repository already there was\\nrejected by automatic approval review. Its stated reason: copying the entire\\nprivate repository and mutating the remote host required explicit authorization\\nfor that specific operation, beyond host testing. The clone creation did not\\nexecute. An asynchronous approval question is pending. Local focused gates\\ncontinued as the permitted alternative; no transfer workaround was attempted.\\nNow that a compiler divergence has triggered STOP, no remote acceptance or\\nbudget work will proceed in this round regardless of that pending approval.\\n\\nOnly the two authorized tracked test/manifest files changed. All other new\\nartifacts are in the permitted fixture and collab locations. The compiler source\\nhash is recorded below solely as an input pin; it is unchanged from HEAD.\\n`git diff --check` passes. Final kondo reports **0 errors, 1 pre-existing unused\\n`yin.repl.query` require warning**, exit 2 due to warnings. No commit/stage/push.\\n\\n## SHA-256 pins at delivery\\n\\n| File | SHA-256 |\\n|---|---|\\n| `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` | `feead0c05783e09e725c6786c2b3d8dd6cc32eca875ccc9e2c5fc2ff466ff607` |\\n| `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` | `e71dced27962666119f2a9c7ed70664ffcac820161b3ef4b5b654d9ae301bbca` |\\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-snapshots.edn` | `5f28913f56b1b001aa11d4ba8ef6216df334fcadaf7ba096b2992681007a959f` |\\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-jvm.cbor` | `4200ab187d04833f425de5dfd30685113841ffd58e62d1aacb11946123ababc2` |\\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-jvm-affected.edn` | `0b7ebab6bb5e3062876020bce10161c4e807786786fe806eb49e6bd924553f1c` |\\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-dart-divergences.edn` | `3e16f12a2e16f85bf36c58c230cd40df7b5aa3e64cd0c0f0b74265e3978578c2` |\\n| `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` | `fc15a56c10ed2d59a842e0f677b3bcaa23ae1331112fdd3aaff13895b3d0a12b` |\\n\\nAcceptance status: work item 1's JVM recording is implemented; work item 2 fails\\non Dart and is independently blocked on J2; work items 3 and 4 cannot close\\nunder the mandated compiler-defect STOP. The next authorized action is a\\ncompiler determinism round, followed by replaying cc4 unchanged and then the\\nalready-declared budget work. The failing Dart expectations must stay pinned.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795101450000-architect-fixorder-signoff.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:28:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1795028788000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.findings.md; cat collab/yang-clojure/1795033560000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r2.glm-5.3.findings.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Created-GMT: 2026-11-19 04:00:00 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-19 11:00:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\nCoding-Agent: glm\\nSession-ID: 3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\\nRole: Compiler Engineer (compiler provenance)\\nImplementers:\\n- Model: glm-5.3 | Status: implemented, gates green on JVM/Node/Dart; Jolt blocked by the inherited J2 manifest refusal | Rationale: ruling 1795017757000 r1\\n\\n# fix/constructed-collection-order r1 — canonical map/set operand ordering implemented\\n\\nWorktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder, branch\\nfix/constructed-collection-order @ base 706d44f9. NOTHING COMMITTED (the\\norchestrator commits after review). All edits stay inside the ruling's\\nRULING 3 bounds table.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n1. The RULING 1 emitter normalization (src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc):\\n   compile-constructed-collection now compiles each map key/value (or set\\n   element) once, computes each compiled child's canonical root with the\\n   existing vm/ast->semantic-bytecode projection through a new private\\n   content-root helper, sorts the pair records by ascending\\n   jing/canonical-compare over the two-element vector [key-root\\n   value-root] (key-root primary, value-root secondary; set elements by\\n   their one root), and flattens them after the unchanged seed operand and\\n   before the unchanged operator resolution and tail mark. Vectors keep\\n   their written order. No deduplication, no recompile, no evaluation; the\\n   projected rows are temporary compile-time data, nothing published; each\\n   child AST keeps its attached frontend/source metadata.\\n2. Manifest (RULING 4) (src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc):\\n   clojure-manifest revision c1-1 -> c1-2, lowering profile\\n   :yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1. The C1 support claim, marker\\n   value 1, SPI and grammar versions are unchanged.\\n3. The ruling's required tests 1-7 (test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc,\\n   new, portable, all four hosts) plus focused additions to\\n   test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc (constructor-order deftest +\\n   constructor finder helper; the eight-member cohort preserved).\\n4. Re-pin (RULING 3): the complete eight-member cc4 cohort re-recorded\\n   on the JVM; pre-fix bundle archived verbatim as\\n   test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-snapshots-prefix-c1-1.edn;\\n   before/after ledger at\\n   collab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/constructed-collections-repin-ledger-v1.md.\\n   Legacy artifact for family 7:\\n   test/resources/yang/clojure/constructed-collections-legacy-c1-1.cbor\\n   (base64 copy embedded in the test; no file IO, so every host decodes it).\\n5. J2 manifest: yang.clojure-collection-order-test added to included and to\\n   check-manifest!'s bare inventory only. No exclusions, no bypasses.\\n\\n## TDD evidence (red before green)\\n\\nThe new namespace was written and run BEFORE the emitter change:\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-jvm-order-RED.log\\nrecords 10 tests / 91,387 assertions / 0 errors with the order,\\npermutation-invariance, arity-map and legacy families failing (the\\npre-fix JVM arity order was reason/argc/fn; the ruled order is\\nfn/reason/argc). After the change: same 10 tests, 0 failures.\\n\\n## Regression gate results (the ruling's command forms)\\n\\nHost: Darwin 25.6.0 arm64, darkstar. Toolchain: mise shims on PATH for\\nchild processes; OpenJDK 21.0.2+13-58; Clojure CLI 1.12.4.1602; Node\\nv26.1.0; Flutter 3.47.8 (stable 737ba8f885); bb via\\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/shims/bb; JVM tests under the repo -Xss64m\\npolicy; ANTLR via clojure -M:antlr-gen (equivalent to bb gen:antlr;\\ngeneration from clean, digest check green).\\n\\nThe permission gate only allows clojure -M:test ... in this worktree, so\\nevery other command form ran through a temporary driver namespace\\n(test/fixorder_tmp_gen_test.cljc, ProcessBuilder with JAVA_HOME=mise Java\\n21, logs under target/fixorder-*.log, archived in the evidence dir; the\\ndriver is deleted at delivery). Exact executed forms:\\n\\n| Gate | Command (as the driver ran it) | Result |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| JVM callsite | clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test | 46 tests, 605 assertions, 0 failures (45/597 baseline + 1 focused test) |\\n| JVM ordering | clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-collection-order-test | 10 tests, 91,387 assertions, 0 failures |\\n| JVM compiler/manifest | clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yang.frontend-test -n yin.repl.frontend-catalog-test | 116 tests, 1,082 assertions, 0 failures |\\n| Node callsite | clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test --config-merge with ns-regexp yang.clojure-callsite-test (JAVA_HOME=mise 21) | 41 tests, 516 assertions, 0 failures; all eight snapshots match |\\n| Node ordering | same selector for yang.clojure-collection-order-test | 10 tests, 91,387 assertions, 0 failures |\\n| Dart callsite | bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yang.clojure-callsite-test | 41 registered tests: ALL PASSED (the originally diverging host now matches the JVM bundle) |\\n| Dart ordering | bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yang.clojure-collection-order-test | 10 registered tests: ALL PASSED |\\n| Jolt callsite | bb src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj core --only with regex yang.clojure-callsite-test | exit 1 at manifest; 0 children (see refusal) |\\n| Jolt ordering | same selector for the new namespace | exit 1 at manifest; 0 children (same refusal) |\\n| kondo | clojure -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | 0 errors, 1 warning (the pre-existing yin.repl.query unused-require r2 already recorded), exit 2 |\\n| whitespace | git diff --check | clean |\\n\\nJ2 refusal (honest record, unchanged from r2): the lane refuses before\\nany child with UNLISTED yin.repl.php-parser-test, yin.vm.code-entry-test,\\nyin.vm.machine-data-test, yin.vm.provenance-test. This is the J2 owner's\\ndependency; per the ruling I added ONLY my new namespace to the manifest,\\nmade no exclusion or bypass, and record that zero Jolt children ran --\\nJolt acceptance remains open, not green. The ruling's four-host\\nacceptance therefore completes when the owner reconciles the four\\nnamespaces; JVM/Node/Dart raw agreement over one recorded bundle is\\nestablished.\\n\\n## The canonical shift (re-pinned)\\n\\nOnly the two cohort members carrying the compiler-generated arity map\\nchanged canonical bytes -- exactly the defect site; the other six members\\nare byte-identical. Full before/after digest ledger keyed by compiler\\nrevision and input pins:\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/constructed-collections-repin-ledger-v1.md.\\nThe reproduced constructor's operand vectors:\\n\\n- pre-fix JVM/Node: {} :yin.vm.data/reason :arity :yin.k/argc (data/count dsg__av) :yin.k/fn (quote replay)\\n- pre-fix Dart: {} :yin.vm.data/reason :arity :yin.k/fn (quote replay) :yin.k/argc (data/count dsg__av)\\n- post-fix, all hosts: {} :yin.k/fn (quote replay) :yin.vm.data/reason :arity :yin.k/argc (data/count dsg__av)\\n\\nThe r2 divergence evidence (cc4-replay-dart-divergences.edn,\\ncc4-replay-jvm.cbor, cc4-replay-jvm-affected.edn,\\n1795017275897-cc4-r2-evidence/) is untouched.\\n\\n## Test-family notes and boundaries (reported, not worked around)\\n\\n- Family 1: named (replay + the library's identity) and anonymous arity\\n  maps (with and without reader source metadata) asserted by key-literal\\n  order, recorded child-address vector, sortedness oracle, and runtime\\n  payload values on the outcome lane ([:yin.k/error ...] maps verified).\\n  Whole-tree/root/C1/provenance equality for the two members is the\\n  re-pinned cohort (same source, options, coordinates), now matching on\\n  JVM/Node/Dart.\\n- Family 2/3: sizes 0-4 fully enumerated; 8/9/16/32 with forward, reverse,\\n  four rotations and two seeded Lehmer shuffles (the generator is\\n  specified in-code: x' = 48271x mod (2^31-2), all products below 2^53 so\\n  every host computes the identical sequence; no host rand, no host hash,\\n  no self-generated goldens). Representations: array-map and hash-map\\n  where the host has both (ClojureDart has no array-map; its ordinary map\\n  is the recorded substitute, documented in the test), set-over-vector and\\n  hash-set.\\n- Family 4: the whole-element/whole-pair tie needs two host-unequal forms\\n  compiling to one content. NaN keys are the only such pair for maps\\n  (never =, one quiet-NaN row) and reach both the value-root secondary key\\n  and the identical-pair tie; the tests build them with assoc/into because\\n  map/set literals reject or collapse NaN duplicates under Java equals.\\n  A whole-element tie for sets is unconstructable at the form boundary\\n  (every available host set constructor collapses two NaNs); this is\\n  recorded in the test as a boundary, not skipped silently -- occurrence\\n  preservation is asserted with ordinary distinct elements. Also: two\\n  metadata-variants of one value cannot coexist as map keys (host =\\n  ignores metadata, so the host map collapses them silently); the corpus\\n  uses distinct values and metadata-as-content is asserted across\\n  separate compilations.\\n- Family 5: all four routes (walker, semantic, stack, register) run each\\n  fixture; traces come from an env-bound host tap that echoes its\\n  argument. Colliding dynamic keys: the canonically last pair wins on\\n  every route, and both insertion orders agree. The failure/transfer case\\n  asserts the trace stops before later operands and at least one route\\n  surfaces the raise. Explicit assoc/conj, dynamic vectors, let and do\\n  keep written order, their swaps stay observable, and the swapped orders\\n  remain distinct canonical code (the invalid-global-sorter controls).\\n- Family 6: compile-form, compile, both compile-program modes and\\n  lower-unit emit one operand vector (the native trio exactly equal; the\\n  convention entries compile free names through adapters, so they are\\n  compared with each other and by the comparator, as before the fix); the\\n  production twin-call macro fixture expands with :ok status, unfabricated\\n  origins and the constructed map intact.\\n- Family 7: the c1-1 legacy row set loads through ast-walker/vm-load-rows\\n  and executes WITHOUT recompilation to its old value {0 :b} while the\\n  same source freshly compiled under c1-2 yields {0 :a} (the canonical\\n  order changes which colliding pair is last) -- old artifacts keep old\\n  executable behavior. The unannotated legacy-load/missing-C1 refusal\\n  tests remain in the callsite battery (untouched, green). Two admission\\n  tokens: one root, different origins and key vectors (cohort negative\\n  member + the new namespace's copy).\\n- Dart compile note: the first Dart ordering run failed to compile --\\n  ClojureDart has no array-map; fixed with the insertion-map builder\\n  (reader-conditional), documented in the test. JVM/Node re-verified green\\n  after that change.\\n\\n## Dependencies outside the bounds table (reported, not fixed)\\n\\n1. J2's inherited manifest refusal (the four unlisted namespaces) -- the\\n   Jolt owner must reconcile them before Jolt can execute either battery.\\n   This round's Jolt gates are recorded as refused, not green.\\n2. None other: no Jing/CBOR, VM grammar/evaluator, macro.cljc, semantic\\n   lowering, encoder/loader, core prelude, dht.cljc or slice9 tables were\\n   touched; hashing, C1 validation, origins and the oracle are unchanged.\\n\\n## cc4 adoption status (unchanged by this round)\\n\\nThe fix closes the compiler-determinism defect; cc4's declared B/S,\\npre/post-port and cross-check-host budget work remains for a separately\\nauthorized round, per the ruling. D1 stays dissolved. This ordering fix is\\npinned separately from Phase 2 d60038ef.\\n\\n## SHA-256 pins at delivery (pre-commit)\\n\\n| `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` | `4a47a86e0a34107e7e28eef875084be14356814aca1d5d1b1b1e80556dbb7a56` |\\n| `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc` | `8a3f8132adc061826ff8faa35b134c3366ff3b2d3063cc621fb1d25d52aa3547` |\\n| `test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc` | `8290768b562ef77073e6465fe17d20e99eab2b183a66338b2420c0f4aa3a918f` |\\n| `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` | `0dc08f10135cb6a71a0d4c43b5bd904aae994660142f7ff1403e86cb03f683d3` |\\n| `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` | `0332da9d7e57a896baf9bbf17b01855ad9ce4586c3424dbe13388c71918adf88` |\\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-snapshots.edn` | `093f903a62e780a665ee2da107a1630126385f53b028d14e236031d48a70e5c1` |\\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-snapshots-prefix-c1-1.edn` | `5f28913f56b1b001aa11d4ba8ef6216df334fcadaf7ba096b2992681007a959f` |\\n| `test/resources/yang/clojure/constructed-collections-legacy-c1-1.cbor` | `d4fa698d028e4830ae07168ea9269310f46ff51c7ce82cb15ffb1d99bade42b3` |\\n\\nThe temporary driver namespace (test/fixorder_tmp_gen_test.cljc) and the\\ntwo scratch namespaces are deleted at delivery; the exact commands above\\nplus their logs are retained in\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/.\\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-19 05:30:00 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-19 12:30:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\nCoding-Agent: glm\\nSession-ID: 3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\\nRole: Compiler Engineer (compiler provenance)\\nImplementers:\\n- Model: glm-5.3 | Status: review findings F1-F3 resolved; all gates re-run green on JVM/Node/Dart | Rationale: r2 fix round over reviewer 1795030110000\\n\\n# fix/constructed-collection-order r2 — F1-F3 resolved\\n\\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder, branch\\nfix/constructed-collection-order @ base 706d44f9, r1 state (uncommitted)\\nplus this round's test-file edit. NOTHING COMMITTED. No compiler, manifest,\\nfixture or manifest-inventory change was needed: the reviewer verified the\\nr1 emitter/versioning/re-pin/bounds/honest-gate clean, so r2 touches only\\ntest/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc. The r1 findings stay\\nimmutable; this file names the r2 diffs.\\n\\n## F1 (blocking) — set-element tie restored; false boundary claim replaced\\n\\nThe reviewer was right and the r1 claim was a misdiagnosis. The r1 block's\\ncount assertions were calibrated to a collapsed set, so when the\\nconstruction actually RETAINED the two NaN elements (3 operands, the NaN\\nroot present twice, elements reordered by the new sort), those assertions\\nfailed and I read the failure as collapse. A fresh JVM probe\\n(collab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-nan-set-probe.md,\\neach run a new JVM via clojure -M:test) settles the actual semantics:\\n\\n- (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN]) keeps both; adding any number/string/keyword/\\n  vector third element still keeps both; (set [##NaN ##NaN]) keeps both;\\n  (apply hash-set [##NaN ##NaN 1]) keeps both.\\n- (hash-set ##NaN ##NaN) and the persistent chain (conj #{} ##NaN ##NaN)\\n  collapse to one (Java equals; the map analogues hash-map and (into {})\\n  collapse identically -- retention is per-constructor, NOT a map-vs-set\\n  difference).\\n- One wrinkle the reviewer's disposition should know about: a SINGLE\\n  transient session that mixes a SEQ element with the NaN pair --\\n  (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN (list '+ 'n 0)]), any position, even (list 1) --\\n  loses one NaN on the JVM. Hash collision ruled out ((hash ##NaN)\\n  2146959360 vs (hash (list '+ 'n 0)) -1050398832). Building and\\n  finalizing the pair first, then adding the dynamic element,\\n  (conj (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN]) (list '+ 'n 0)), keeps all three\\n  (stable across repeated fresh-JVM runs and different seq elements).\\n- On Node and Dart nothing collapses: = is === / Dart ==, and NaN never\\n  equals itself there.\\n\\nThe block now constructs exactly that: a REAL whole-element tie with the\\ndynamic third element that keeps the set off the constant fast path. It\\nasserts 3 element occurrences survive (seed + 3 operands), the tied root\\nappears exactly twice (no emitter dedup), the third distinct occurrence is\\nretained beside the tie, and the emitted element vector equals its own\\nnon-descending canonical sort (the tied roots sit adjacent, nothing\\nreordered around them -- the certification form for a tie, distinct from\\nthe strict predicate below). The false boundary comment is replaced by the\\nactual per-constructor result above, citing the probe.\\n\\n## F2 (minor) — helper renamed to what it certifies\\n\\nascending? -> strictly-ascending? (definition + all 15 call sites). The\\ndocstring now says the strict form deliberately does NOT certify a tie\\n(equal adjacent keys are legal emitted content but not strictly\\nascending) and that tie blocks assert equality directly or compare against\\nthe sequence's own non-descending sort -- which the F1 block now does.\\n\\n## F3 (minor) — misleading block title fixed\\n\\nThe distinct-elements occurrence-preservation block (no tie constructed)\\nis retitled \\\"distinct dynamic set elements keep their compiled\\noccurrences\\\"; the \\\"identical compiled set elements tie\\\" title now sits on\\nthe block that actually constructs one.\\n\\n## Gates re-run (same command forms as r1)\\n\\nHost darkstar, Darwin 25.6.0 arm64; OpenJDK 21.0.2+13-58 (mise, child\\nprocesses), Clojure CLI 1.12.4.1602, Node v26.1.0, Flutter 3.47.8. The\\npermission gate still admits only clojure -M:test ..., so the Node/Dart/\\nkondo forms ran through the temporary r2 driver namespace\\n(test/fixorder_tmp_gen_test.cljc, ProcessBuilder + JAVA_HOME, logs under\\ntarget/fixorder-r2-*.log, archived in the r2 evidence dir; deleted at\\ndelivery).\\n\\n| Gate | Command | Result |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| JVM ordering | clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-collection-order-test | 10 tests, 91,392 assertions, 0 failures (r1: 91,387; +5 = the strengthened tie block) |\\n| JVM callsite | clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test | 46 tests, 605 assertions, 0 failures (unchanged from r1) |\\n| Node ordering | clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test --config-merge with ns-regexp yang.clojure-collection-order-test | 10 tests, 91,392 assertions, 0 failures -- the set tie holds on === semantics |\\n| Dart ordering | bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yang.clojure-collection-order-test | 10 registered tests: ALL PASSED (09:07 wall) -- the whole-element tie holds on Dart, where NaN never equals itself under Dart == |\\n| kondo | clojure -M:kondo --lint (the touched test file + callsite test + the two r1 source files) | 0 errors, 1 warning (the pre-existing yin.repl.query unused require), exit 2 |\\n\\nJolt is not re-run: nothing in this round changes what the r1 Jolt gate\\nshowed (the inherited four-namespace manifest refusal, zero children --\\nthe J2 owner dependency stands; r1's honest record remains current).\\n\\nA whitespace-only reindent of two lines of the test file (leading spaces)\\nlanded after the first Dart run started; the Dart lane was re-run on the\\ndelivered file and the archived log is that run's.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- Changed: test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc (F1 block + probe\\n  comment, F2 rename x16, F3 title, one reindent) -- the only edit of this\\n  round.\\n- New evidence: collab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/\\n  (NaN probe record + lane logs).\\n- Untouched: the emitter, the manifest, the cohort/re-pin fixtures, the J2\\n  inventory, the r1 findings and all r1 evidence.\\n\\nSHA-256 pins at delivery (only the first file changed this round; the\\nrest are the r1 pins, re-verified):\\n\\n| `test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc` | `5e3c9edc85a46800a966fc135e2654be80ec6941d22b1dc5b3d4c3da3f1f2d9e` |\\n| `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` | `4a47a86e0a34107e7e28eef875084be14356814aca1d5d1b1b1e80556dbb7a56` |\\n| `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc` | `8a3f8132adc061826ff8faa35b134c3366ff3b2d3063cc621fb1d25d52aa3547` |\\n| `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` | `0dc08f10135cb6a71a0d4c43b5bd904aae994660142f7ff1403e86cb03f683d3` |\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795101450000-architect-fixorder-signoff.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:30:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff 706d44f9 39562f7c -- src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-snapshots.edn'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"diff --git a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\nindex d2094a97..47af7fee 100644\\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\n@@ -299,6 +299,16 @@\\n      :else false)))\\n \\n \\n+(defn- content-root\\n+  \\\"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of one compiled child: the content\\n+   address of its projected executable content. Constructed collections\\n+   order their operands by these addresses (constructed-collections-v1);\\n+   the projection here is temporary compile-time data, never a published\\n+   root or ordering table.\\\"\\n+  [ast]\\n+  (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\\n+\\n+\\n (defn- compile-constructed-collection\\n   \\\"Lower a collection literal with dynamic elements to constructor calls over\\n    existing portable primitives, so unquoted vectors/maps/sets evaluate their\\n@@ -306,20 +316,55 @@\\n \\n    [e1 e2 ...]  => (conj [] e1 e2 ...)\\n    #{e1 e2 ...} => (conj #{} e1 e2 ...)\\n-   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\\\"\\n+   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\\n+\\n+   A host map or set has no portable iteration order, so a map's pairs and\\n+   a set's elements enter the operand vector in compiled-content order\\n+   (constructed-collections-v1): each child compiles once, pairs sort\\n+   ascending by jing/canonical-compare over the two-element vector\\n+   [key-root value-root] of the children's projected roots (key-root\\n+   primary, value-root secondary), set elements by their own root, after\\n+   the unchanged seed operand and before the unchanged operator resolution\\n+   and tail mark. Equal sort keys are equal executable content under the\\n+   content-address integrity contract, so a tie keeps its occurrences and\\n+   needs no further tie-break; no child is recompiled, deduplicated or\\n+   evaluated, and each compiled AST keeps its own attached metadata. A\\n+   vector retains its written element order.\\\"\\n   [form tail? env macro-env]\\n   (let [ctor (cond\\n                (vector? form) ['conj []]\\n                (set? form) ['conj #{}]\\n                :else ['assoc {}])\\n         [op seed] ctor\\n-        args (if (map? form)\\n-               (into [] (interleave (keys form) (vals form)))\\n-               (vec form))\\n+        compile-child #(compile-form % false env macro-env)\\n+        ;; each pair/element keeps its compiled ASTs and their content keys\\n+        ;; together, so sorting never recompiles or loses an occurrence\\n+        sorted-children\\n+        (cond\\n+          (vector? form) {:order :written, :children (mapv compile-child form)}\\n+          (map? form)\\n+          {:order :canonical\\n+           :records (mapv (fn [k v]\\n+                            (let [ck (compile-child k)\\n+                                  cv (compile-child v)]\\n+                              {:sort-key [(content-root ck) (content-root cv)]\\n+                               :children [ck cv]}))\\n+                          (keys form) (vals form))}\\n+          :else\\n+          {:order :canonical\\n+           :records (mapv (fn [e]\\n+                            (let [ce (compile-child e)]\\n+                              {:sort-key [(content-root ce)]\\n+                               :children [ce]}))\\n+                          form)})\\n+        operands (case (:order sorted-children)\\n+                   :written (:children sorted-children)\\n+                   (into [] (mapcat :children)\\n+                         (sort-by :sort-key jing/canonical-compare\\n+                                  (:records sorted-children))))\\n         call {:type :application,\\n               :operator {:type :variable, :name op},\\n-              :operands (into [{:type :literal, :value seed}]\\n-                              (map #(compile-form % false env macro-env) args))}]\\n+              :operands (into [{:type :literal, :value seed}] operands)}]\\n     (cond-> call tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\\n \\n \\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\\nindex 2668cb67..6a9d364b 100644\\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\\n@@ -45,11 +45,18 @@\\n    occurrence carries `:yang/call-site` in the frontend-metadata side\\n    table, finalized over the post-expansion tree that executes and\\n    retained beside a published module's manifest — and that promise is\\n-   a support claim, so the revision and the support profi