} ##NaN ##NaN))                      1 nan=1  collapses (persistent chain)\\n;;   (count (conj (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN]) app))         3 nan=2  KEEPS (chosen)\\n;;   (count (into (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN]) [app]))       3 nan=2  KEEPS\\n;;   map analogues: (assoc {} ##NaN 1 ##NaN 2)           2 nan=2  keeps (r1 map tie)\\n;;                  (hash-map ##NaN :l ##NaN :r)         1 nan=1  collapses\\n;;                  (into {} [[##NaN v] [##NaN v]])      collapses (r1 observation)\\n;;\\n;; Hash collision ruled out: (hash ##NaN) = 2146959360,\\n;; (hash (list '+ 'n 0)) = -1050398832. The trigger for the single-session\\n;; loss is the seq element itself (also (list 1) loses), not its bucket.\\n;;\\n;; Conclusion: the whole-element tie IS constructable; retention is\\n;; per-constructor (JVM transient/persistent/check paths differ), not a\\n;; map-vs-set difference. The r1 \\\"unconstructable\\\" claim was a\\n;; misdiagnosis: the r1 block's count assertions were calibrated to a\\n;; collapsed set, and their failure (3 operands, NaN root seen twice)\\n;; actually demonstrated retention with reordering. Reviewer F1 sustained.\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-kondo.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-nan-set-probe.md\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-jvm-order.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-jvm-callsite.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-dart-order.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-node-order.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794932781000-cc4-partial-findings.md\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-node-callsite.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-node-order.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-dart-order.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder