97-cc4-r2-evidence/cc4-r2-node-final.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795017275897-cc4-r2-evidence/cc4-r2-jvm.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795017275897-cc4-r2-evidence/cc4-r2-minimal-row-diff.edn\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795017275897-cc4-r2-evidence/capture-jvm.clj\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795017275897-cc4-r2-evidence/cc4-r2-node.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795017275897-cc4-r2-evidence/cc4-r2-common-operands.edn\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795017275897-cc4-r2-evidence/cc4-r2-dart-retry.log\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795017484194-engineer-cc4-r2-findings.md\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794513111000-engineer-cc4-fourhost-equality-budget.prompt.md\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795016601236-cc4-r2-budget-declaration-v1.md\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795033560000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r2.glm-5.3.findings.md\\ncollab/exception-track/1794484000000-to-yangclojure-cc4-coordination.md\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795101450000-architect-fixorder-signoff.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:34:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,265p' test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"(ns yang.clojure-collection-order-test\\n  \\\"Constructed collections v1 (architect ruling 1795017757000, RULING 1-4):\\n   the canonical operand ordering of dynamically constructed map and set\\n   literals at yang.clojure's collection emitter, the evaluation semantics\\n   that ordering makes executable, and the manifest/legacy boundaries of the\\n   c1-2 revision.\\n\\n   Every order expectation here comes from builders independent of the\\n   emitter's own sort: children project through\\n   yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode and order through dao.jing/canonical-compare\\n   (RFC 8949 canonical bytes, unsigned bytewise, proper prefix first), the\\n   same comparator the ruling names -- never through the helper under test.\\\"\\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\n            [dao.stream.base64 :as base64]\\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\\n            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\\n            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Independent oracle builders (RULING 1's comparator, not the emitter's sort)\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n(defn- collection-applications\\n  \\\"Every constructor application of compiled `ast` -- an assoc over the {}\\n   seed or a conj over the []/#{} seed -- in outermost-first walk order. A\\n   program under test contains either only emitter output or only the\\n   explicit constructor calls a control names, never both.\\\"\\n  [ast]\\n  (let [acc (atom [])]\\n    (walk/postwalk\\n      (fn [n]\\n        (when (and (map? n)\\n                   (= :application (:type n))\\n                   (= :variable (get-in n [:operator :type]))\\n                   (= :literal (get-in n [:operands 0 :type]))\\n                   (contains? #{[(quote assoc) {}] [(quote conj) []] [(quote conj) #{}]}\\n                              [(get-in n [:operator :name])\\n                               (get-in n [:operands 0 :value])]))\\n          (swap! acc conj n))\\n        n)\\n      ast)\\n    @acc))\\n\\n\\n(defn- child-roots\\n  \\\"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of each operand of `node`,\\n   projected independently of the emitter.\\\"\\n  [node]\\n  (mapv (fn [o] (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode o))) (:operands node)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- map-constructors\\n  [ast]\\n  (into [] (filter #(= (quote assoc) (get-in % [:operator :name])))\\n        (collection-applications ast)))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private empty-map-seed-root\\n  \\\"The content address of the {} seed literal: host- and revision-stable.\\\"\\n  :segment/blake3-201f235cbac998f43954454e9df0eb633717e79de535776f3f51e198a3759b10)\\n\\n\\n(defn- pair-keys\\n  \\\"The RULING 1 sort keys of a map constructor's pairs: `[key-root\\n   value-root]` per source pair, in emitted order.\\\"\\n  [node]\\n  (mapv vec (partition 2 (rest (child-roots node)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- element-keys\\n  \\\"The RULING 1 sort keys of a set constructor's elements (one root each),\\n   in emitted order.\\\"\\n  [node]\\n  (mapv vector (rest (child-roots node))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- strictly-ascending?\\n  \\\"True when `ks` sorts strictly ascending by jing/canonical-compare: every\\n   adjacent pair compares negative. The strict form deliberately does NOT\\n   certify a tie (equal adjacent keys are equal executable content and a\\n   legal emitted order, but not a strictly ascending one) -- blocks that\\n   construct a tie assert it directly or compare against the sequence's\\n   own non-descending sort instead.\\\"\\n  [ks]\\n  (every? (fn [[a b]] (neg? (jing/canonical-compare a b)))\\n          (partition 2 1 ks)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- key-literals\\n  \\\"The literal values at the key positions of a map constructor (every\\n   second operand after the seed), for reading an emitted order.\\\"\\n  [node]\\n  (mapv (fn [o] (when (= :literal (:type o)) (:value o)))\\n        (take-nth 2 (rest (:operands node)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- project-batch\\n  \\\"One compiled ast through the production encoder envelope under `token`.\\\"\\n  ([ast] (project-batch ast \\\"order-a\\\"))\\n  ([ast token]\\n   (let [p (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope :cc4/replay token [ast]))]\\n     {:tree (first (:yin/batch p))\\n      :rows (:yin/frontend-metadata p)})))\\n\\n\\n(defn- digest-snapshot\\n  \\\"The equality snapshot of one projected batch: root, the canonical-sorted\\n   C1 marker relation, the sorted occurrence-key vector, and all three\\n   instruction formats' call-provenance -- the cohort's model, with nothing\\n   normalized away.\\\"\\n  [{:keys [tree rows]}]\\n  (let [c1 (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\\n                      (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)) rows)))\\n        keys (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\\n                        (into [] (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\\n                                       (map #(vec (take 3 %)))) rows)))\\n        sem (linearize/project-rows tree nil rows)\\n        stack (derive/stack-image (:vector sem)\\n                                  {:segment-address :order/stack\\n                                   :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})\\n        register (derive/register-image (:vector sem)\\n                                        {:segment-address :order/register\\n                                         :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})]\\n    {:root (:root tree)\\n     :applications (count keys)\\n     :keys-digest (jing/content-hash keys)\\n     :c1-digest (jing/content-hash c1)\\n     :instruction-provenance-digest\\n     (jing/content-hash [(:call-provenance sem)\\n                         (:call-provenance stack)\\n                         (:call-provenance register)])}))\\n\\n\\n(defn- compile-snapshot\\n  \\\"Compile `form`, project it, digest it.\\\"\\n  [form]\\n  (digest-snapshot (project-batch (yang/compile form))))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Execution routes (RULING 2/3: walker, semantic, stack, register)\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n(def ^:private registry\\n  (-> (module/empty-registry)\\n      module/register-cell-module\\n      data/register-data-module))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private base-opts\\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream\\n   :capability-secret tu/secret\\n   :primitives vm/primitives\\n   :modules registry})\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private load-semantic-ast\\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private lanes\\n  \\\"The four execution routes the behavior tests run.\\\"\\n  [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\\n\\n\\n(defn- run-lane\\n  \\\"Run compiled `ast` on one execution route.\\\"\\n  [lane ast env]\\n  ;; the walker/semantic machines take :env; the debruijn machines take\\n  ;; :free-env for free names -- both spell the same test-supplied bindings\\n  (let [opts (assoc base-opts :env env :free-env env)]\\n    (case lane\\n      :ast-walker (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast)\\n      :semantic (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\\n                                           (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\\n      :stack (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\\n                       (:image (derive/stack-image\\n                                 (:vector (linearize/project ast))))\\n                       (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract)))\\n      :register (vm/run (rvm/create-vm\\n                          (derive/register-image\\n                            (:vector (linearize/project ast)))\\n                          (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- run-on\\n  \\\"Run compiled `ast` on every execution route with `env`, returning\\n   lane -> value.\\\"\\n  ([ast] (run-on ast {}))\\n  ([ast env]\\n   (into {} (map (fn [lane] [lane (vm/value (run-lane lane ast env))]))\\n         lanes)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- run-form\\n  \\\"Compile and run `form` on every route with `env`.\\\"\\n  ([form] (run-form form {}))\\n  ([form env] (run-on (yang/compile form) env)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- trace-of\\n  \\\"The observable evaluation of `form` on every route: the lane's value\\n   (or its raised ex-data) together with the ordered log the env-bound\\n   `tap` host function recorded during THAT lane's run. `tap` echoes its\\n   argument, so a log is exactly the order that lane consumed the operands\\n   in; a lane whose operand raises still reports the events that happened\\n   before the raise.\\\"\\n  [form env]\\n  (let [ast (yang/compile form)\\n        log (atom [])\\n        env (assoc env (quote tap) (fn [x] (swap! log conj x) x))]\\n    (into {} (map (fn [lane]\\n                    (reset! log [])\\n                    (let [result (try\\n                                   {:value (vm/value (run-lane lane ast env))}\\n                                   (catch #?(:clj Exception, :cljs :default, :cljd Object) e\\n                                     {:raised (ex-data e)}))]\\n                      [lane (assoc result :log @log)])))\\n          lanes)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- permutations-of\\n  \\\"Every ordering of the items, the plain recursive enumeration.\\\"\\n  [items]\\n  (if (empty? items)\\n    [[]]\\n    (mapcat (fn [i]\\n              (map (fn [rest-perm] (into [i] rest-perm))\\n                   (permutations-of (vec (remove #{i} items)))))\\n            items)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- all-permutations\\n  \\\"Every ordering of (range n).\\\"\\n  [n]\\n  (permutations-of (vec (range n))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- rotate\\n  \\\"The kth rotation of `v`.\\\"\\n  [k v]\\n  (let [k (mod k (count v))]\\n    (into (subvec v k) (subvec v 0 k))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- lcg\\n  \\\"The recorded-seed Lehmer generator x' = 48271*x mod (2^31-2). Every\\n   product stays below 2^53, so every host computes the identical sequence\\n   in its double arithmetic (a long-math generator would not be portable).\\\"\\n  [seed n]\\n  (loop [out [] x seed i 0]\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795101450000-architect-fixorder-signoff.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:37:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff 706d44f9 39562f7c -- src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj; git show --format=fuller --no-patch 706d44f9 39562f7c 7e6d720c; git diff --name-status 39562f7c 7e6d720c -- src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc test/resources/yang/clojure'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"diff --git a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\nindex d2094a97..47af7fee 100644\\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\n@@ -299,6 +299,16 @@\\n      :else false)))\\n \\n \\n+(defn- content-root\\n+  \\\"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of one compiled child: the content\\n+   address of its projected executable content. Constructed collections\\n+   order their operands by these addresses (constructed-collections-v1);\\n+   the projection here is temporary compile-time data, never a published\\n+   root or ordering table.\\\"\\n+  [ast]\\n+  (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\\n+\\n+\\n (defn- compile-constructed-collection\\n   \\\"Lower a collection literal with dynamic elements to constructor calls over\\n    existing portable primitives, so unquoted vectors/maps/sets evaluate their\\n@@ -306,20 +316,55 @@\\n \\n    [e1 e2 ...]  => (conj [] e1 e2 ...)\\n    #{e1 e2 ...} => (conj #{} e1 e2 ...)\\n-   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\\\"\\n+   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\\n+\\n+   A host map or set has no portable iteration order, so a map's pairs and\\n+   a set's elements enter the operand vector in compiled-content order\\n+   (constructed-collections-v1): each child compiles once, pairs sort\\n+   ascending by jing/canonical-compare over the two-element vector\\n+   [key-root value-root] of the children's projected roots (key-root\\n+   primary, value-root secondary), set elements by their own root, after\\n+   the unchanged seed operand and before the unchanged operator resolution\\n+   and tail mark. Equal sort keys are equal executable content under the\\n+   content-address integrity contract, so a tie keeps its occurrences and\\n+   needs no further tie-break; no child is recompiled, deduplicated or\\n+   evaluated, and each compiled AST keeps its own attached metadata. A\\n+   vector retains its written element order.\\\"\\n   [form tail? env macro-env]\\n   (let [ctor (cond\\n                (vector? form) ['conj []]\\n                (set? form) ['conj #{}]\\n                :else ['assoc {}])\\n         [op seed] ctor\\n-        args (if (map? form)\\n-               (into [] (interleave (keys form) (vals form)))\\n-               (vec form))\\n+        compile-child #(compile-form % false env macro-env)\\n+        ;; each pair/element keeps its compiled ASTs and their content keys\\n+        ;; together, so sorting never recompiles or loses an occurrence\\n+        sorted-children\\n+        (cond\\n+          (vector? form) {:order :written, :children (mapv compile-child form)}\\n+          (map? form)\\n+          {:order :canonical\\n+           :records (mapv (fn [k v]\\n+                            (let [ck (compile-child k)\\n+                                  cv (compile-child v)]\\n+                              {:sort-key [(content-root ck) (content-root cv)]\\n+                               :children [ck cv]}))\\n+                          (keys form) (vals form))}\\n+          :else\\n+          {:order :canonical\\n+           :records (mapv (fn [e]\\n+                            (let [ce (compile-child e)]\\n+                              {:sort-key [(content-root ce)]\\n+                               :children [ce]}))\\n+                          form)})\\n+        operands (case (:order sorted-children)\\n+                   :written (:children sorted-children)\\n+                   (into [] (mapcat :children)\\n+                         (sort-by :sort-key jing/canonical-compare\\n+                                  (:records sorted-children))))\\n         call {:type :application,\\n               :operator {:type :variable, :name op},\\n-              :operands (into [{:type :literal, :value seed}]\\n-                              (map #(compile-form % false env macro-env) args))}]\\n+              :operands (into [{:type :literal, :value seed}] operands)}]\\n     (cond-> call tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\\n \\n \\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\\nindex 2668cb67..6a9d364b 100644\\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\\n@@ -45,11 +45,18 @@\\n    occurrence carries `:yang/call-site` in the frontend-metadata side\\n    table, finalized over the post-expansion tree that executes and\\n    retained beside a published module's manifest — and that promise is\\n-   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it;\\n-   the shared legacy profiles no longer describe this frontend.\\\"\\n+   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it.\\n+   Revision c1-2 additionally declares the constructed-collections\\n+   lowering profile: a dynamically constructed map or set literal now\\n+   orders its constructor operands by compiled content\\n+   (:yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1), a one-time canonical\\n+   shift for affected newly compiled artifacts; the C1 support claim,\\n+   the C1 marker value and the execution grammar versions are\\n+   unchanged.\\\"\\n   []\\n   (assoc (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\\n-         :yang.frontend/revision \\\"c1-1\\\"\\n+         :yang.frontend/revision \\\"c1-2\\\"\\n+         :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1\\n          :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1))\\n \\n \\ndiff --git a/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj b/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\\nindex d0b316de..4fbfe588 100644\\n--- a/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\\n+++ b/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\\n@@ -347,7 +347,10 @@\\n    \\\"yin.vm.ucf.fencing-rows-test\\\" \\\"yin.vm.ucf.holder.reader-test\\\"\\n    \\\"yin.vm.ucf.holder.writer-test\\\" \\\"yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver-test\\\"\\n    ;; cc4: the frontend's own replay-equality gate is mandatory on Jolt.\\n-   \\\"yang.clojure-callsite-test\\\"])\\n+   \\\"yang.clojure-callsite-test\\\"\\n+   ;; constructed-collections-v1 (fix round, ruling 1795017757000): the\\n+   ;; canonical operand-ordering battery.\\n+   \\\"yang.clojure-collection-order-test\\\"])\\n \\n \\n ;; Read only namespace tokens, never evaluate forms or resolve reader branches.\\n@@ -358,7 +361,7 @@\\n   [test-root included-nses excluded-suites]\\n   (let [dirs [\\\"dao/host\\\" \\\"dao/jing\\\" \\\"dao/data\\\" \\\"dao/space\\\" \\\"dao/stream\\\" \\\"yin/vm\\\" \\\"yin/repl\\\"]\\n         bare [\\\"dao/jing_test\\\" \\\"dao/stream_test\\\" \\\"dao/data_test\\\" \\\"yin/vm_test\\\" \\\"yin/repl_test\\\"\\n-              \\\"yang/clojure_callsite_test\\\"]\\n+              \\\"yang/clojure_callsite_test\\\" \\\"yang/clojure_collection_order_test\\\"]\\n         extensions [\\\"clj\\\" \\\"cljc\\\" \\\"cljs\\\" \\\"cljd\\\"]\\n         files (->> (concat\\n                      (mapcat #(->> (fs/glob (fs/path test-root %) \\\"**\\\")\\ncommit 706d44f9c2f46d0959b88e68f82e8bb3e98cefd0\\nAuthor:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\\nAuthorDate: Wed Nov 18 23:13:07 2026 +0700\\nCommit:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\\nCommitDate: Wed Nov 18 23:13:07 2026 +0700\\n\\n    test(cc4): the four-host C1 replay-equality gate — reproduced Dart constructed-map divergence\\n    \\n    r1+r2 of the cc4 acceptance round (uncommitted until now so the authorized\\n    determinism fix round can branch from this base). Contains the strengthened\\n    callsite battery, the pinned eight-member replay cohort, the divergence\\n    evidence, and the pre-declared budget ceilings v1. Verdict FAIL per the\\n    brief's STOP rule: compile-constructed-collection emits host map iteration\\n    order into canonical operands (ruling 1795017757000 governs the repair).\\n    No compiler source changed. No commits to master.\\n\\ncommit 39562f7cafee446b3d1f43197415de29871b5306\\nAuthor:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\\nAuthorDate: Thu Nov 19 03:53:00 2026 +0700\\nCommit:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\\nCommitDate: Thu Nov 19 03:53:00 2026 +0700\\n\\n    fix(yang): canonical ordering for constructed map/set operands — ruling 1795017757000\\n    \\n    compile-constructed-collection sorts map pairs by ascending\\n    jing/canonical-compare of [key-root value-root] (roots from the existing\\n    vm/ast->semantic-bytecode projection) and set elements by their element\\n    root; vectors keep written order; no dedup; seeds and operator resolution\\n    unchanged. Manifest c1-1 -> c1-2, profile :yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1.\\n    Fixes the reproduced Dart divergence from cc4 r2 (host map iteration order\\n    leaking into canonical operands).\\n    \\n    - new portable suite yang.clojure-collection-order-test (ruling test families 1-7,\\n      incl. the set-element tie per reviewer disposition r2); the raw RED-run log\\n      (126.5 MB) exceeds GitHub's file limit and stays untracked in the authoring\\n      worktree — a sha-pinned digest stands in the evidence dir\\n    - complete cc4 cohort re-pinned; pre-fix bundle archived (sha 5f28913f preserved);\\n      before/after ledger + NaN-set probe evidence under collab/yang-clojure/\\n    - J2 manifest: only the new namespace added; the four inherited unlisted\\n      namespaces remain the J2 owner's dependency\\n    \\n    Reviewer: deepseek-v4-pro APPROVE (r1 CHANGES-REQUIRED -> r2 confirmed).\\n    Gates: JVM 46/605 + 10/91,392 + compiler 116/1,082; Node 41/516 + 10/91,392;\\n    Dart 41 + 10 all-pass; Jolt blocked by inherited J2 refusal (recorded).\\n\\ncommit 7e6d720c8a745b6366643a7e1388b4e4380ead79\\nMerge: 39562f7c 657f01ff\\nAuthor:     Sonny To 