 \\\"ODc5\\\"]))\\n\\n\\n(defn- legacy-payload\\n  \\\"The decoded pre-fix artifact.\\\"\\n  []\\n  (cbor/decode (base64/decode legacy-c1-1-payload-b64)))\\n\\n\\n(deftest legacy-artifact-loads-and-runs-test\\n  \\\"RULING 4: a retained pre-fix artifact loads at its old address and\\n   executes without recompilation, keeping its old operand order and old\\n   behavior; the same source freshly compiled under c1-2 canonicalizes.\\\"\\n  (let [payload (legacy-payload)\\n        rows (select-keys payload [:root :rows])\\n        program (list (list (quote fn) [(quote x)]\\n                            (insertion-map\\n                              [(list (quote -) (quote x) 1) :a\\n                               (list (quote -) 1 (quote x)) :b]))\\n                      1)\\n        recompiled (yang/compile program)]\\n    (testing \\\"the artifact is complete and self-consistent\\\"\\n      (is (= (:root payload) (get-in payload [:rows (:root payload) 0])))\\n      (is (= \\\"c1-1\\\" (:manifest-revision payload))))\\n    (testing \\\"the rows load through the walker loader and run unchanged\\\"\\n      (let [vm (ast-walker/vm-load-rows (tu/create-vm base-opts)\\n                                        rows vm/ast-contract)]\\n        (is (= (:old-value payload) (vm/value (vm/run vm)))\\n            \\\"old operand order stays old executable behavior\\\")))\\n    (testing \\\"the old order is not the new canonical order\\\"\\n      (is (pos? (count (get-in payload [:old-operand-roots]))))\\n      (is (not= (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode recompiled))\\n                (:root payload))\\n          \\\"recompiling the same source mints the canonicalized tree\\\"))\\n    (testing \\\"the fresh compilation canonicalizes and changes the winner\\\"\\n      (let [ctor (first (map-constructors recompiled))]\\n        (is (strictly-ascending? (pair-keys ctor)))\\n        (is (not= (child-roots ctor)\\n                  (vec (:old-operand-roots payload))))\\n        ;; both keys evaluate to 0; the canonically last pair wins now\\n        (is (= (:old-value payload) {0 :b}))\\n        (is (not= {0 :b} (:ast-walker (run-form program {}))))))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest token-admission-distinct-origins-test\\n  \\\"Admitting the same content under two tokens yields one root and two\\n   distinct origin sets and occurrence-key vectors (the cohort negative\\n   member rule).\\\"\\n  (let [form {(list (quote tap) :k) (list (quote tap) :v)}\\n        a (project-batch (yang/compile form) \\\"order-a\\\")\\n        b (project-batch (yang/compile form) \\\"order-b\\\")\\n        origins (fn [batch]\\n                  (into #{} (comp (filter (fn [row] (= :yang/call-site (nth row 3))))\\n                                  (map first))\\n                        (:rows batch)))]\\n    (is (= (:root (:tree a)) (:root (:tree b))))\\n    (is (not= (origins a) (origins b)))\\n    (is (not= (digest-snapshot a) (digest-snapshot b)))))\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795101450000-architect-fixorder-signoff.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:64:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_32\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,95p' collab/yang-clojure/1795016601236-cc4-r2-budget-declaration-v1.md; sed -n '1,110p' collab/yang-clojure/1794513111000-engineer-cc4-fourhost-equality-budget.prompt.md; cat collab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-jvm-compiler.log collab/yang-clojure/1795028800000-fixorder-evidence/fixorder-node-callsite.log; tail -5 collab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-dart-order.log\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Created-GMT: 2026-11-18 15:43:21 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-18 22:43:21 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\nCoding-Agent: codex\\nSession-ID: 01a1ea51-a87d-7062-ae12-e6c1c169b48c\\n\\n# cc4 r2 bounded run declaration v1 (before budget measurements)\\n\\nRevision: post `2687ab0cf03ebaa232be49a2333347d12a71d9a3` plus the cc4 test-only patch;\\npre-port `8afd82f5e99d0f2b2d38a5f53b292105fdead688` (first parent of\\nport merge `309fe842`). Input corpus: the eight entries in `replay-artifacts`\\nin `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`: destructuring/float/metadata/duplicate\\nnative and argument-vector programs, lower-unit with bundled library, prelude,\\nmacro twin with its producing log, second-token admission, and freshly published\\n`yang.call` and `clj` with their complete side artifacts. No runtime tracing.\\n\\nThe cc3 v2.1 baselines are reference observations, NOT cc4 measurements:\\nrows 312886 B, relation 856315 B, retained compiled-inclusive maximum\\n8924640 B, peak 272026880 B, pipeline maximum 772 ms. Its per-fixture ceilings\\nwere 2 MB/artifact, 4 MB/aggregate, 12 MB retained, 1 GiB peak, 10 s pipeline.\\nThe following finite ceilings scale these to an eight-member closure and allow\\nhost representation differences. A sample exceeding a bound FAILS this run;\\nno bound will be raised in place.\\n\\n| Quantity | Finite ceiling, both revisions, every host/configuration |\\n|---|---:|\\n| Unique canonical rows / occurrence positions / application positions, corpus | 50000 / 100000 / 10000 |\\n| Maximum path depth / encoded application paths, corpus | 256 / 8000000 B |\\n| Static side bytes per artifact / aggregate closure | 2000000 B / 32000000 B |\\n| Aggregate retained compiled-inclusive holder | 96000000 B incremental used heap |\\n| Absolute sampled heap peak | 2147483648 B |\\n| Absolute process-tree RSS peak, where heap unavailable | 4294967296 B |\\n| Retained process RSS, where heap unavailable | 4294967296 B (absolute; not heap-comparable) |\\n| Warm pipeline / cold pipeline (excludes toolchain compilation) | 80000 / 160000 ms |\\n| Each compile/expand/project/publish/load/query stage | 80000 ms |\\n| S−B allowed pipeline / retained / aggregate static bytes | 40000 ms / 96000000 B / 32000000 B |\\n| Trace records / capacity / trace bytes | 0 / 0 / 0 (trace disabled throughout) |\\n\\nStorage aggregate uses 8 × cc3's 4 MB ceiling; retained uses 8 × 12 MB.\\nPeak heap uses 2 × cc3's 1 GiB ceiling; process RSS includes runtime/native\\nallocator/executable pages and therefore has a separately named 4 GiB ceiling.\\nWarm time uses 8 × 10 s; cold time is twice warm. Depth and input limits are\\nconservative finite preflight rejection bounds for this small pinned corpus,\\nincluding generated/prelude closure. No tagged execution is part of cc4.\\n\\nB uses the same compiling inputs with C1 metadata removed before projection,\\nlowering/publication/persistence/load/query; S retains annotations and enables\\nthose side operations. Both disable runtime trace. The production compiler\\ncurrently always annotates: the compile cost common to B/S includes that work.\\nS−B therefore measures downstream static-artifact overhead and cannot establish\\nthe annotation producer's incremental compile cost. This limitation must appear\\nwith the result; no claim of total zero compile overhead is permitted.\\n\\nProcedure: one cold build, one discarded warmup, 3 warm pipeline samples per\\nconfiguration; 5 retained samples where forced GC is available (JVM and Node).\\nHold one complete corpus at a time, release each holder before the next sample.\\nRecord every sample and use MAXIMUM for every verdict. JVM: GC-pinned\\nRuntime totalMemory−freeMemory, 2 ms sampled used heap. Node: exposed GC,\\nprocess.memoryUsage().heapUsed and synchronous stage-boundary heap samples\\n(mark as a lower bound on the true transient peak). Dart/Jolt: named process RSS\\nif heap counters are unavailable; process RSS is never substituted for a heap\\ndelta without recording the changed metric. Warm time excludes toolchain build;\\nclass-loading/startup must be identified separately. Measure pre and post using\\nthe same harness and inputs; any pre/post shift is allocated to port Phase 2\\n`d60038ef` as directed, with unrelated base differences stated as confounders.\\nD1 is dissolved and no correspondence acceptance is claimed.\\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-12 19:11:51 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-13 02:11:51 +0700\\nCoding-Agent: TBD-ON-DISPATCH\\nSession-ID: TBD-ON-DISPATCH\\n\\n# Task: cc4 — the four-host Clojure C1 replay-equality gate & budget record\\n\\nRole: VM Engineer (compiler provenance)\\n\\nImplementers:\\n- Model: TBD-ON-DISPATCH | Assigned: PARKED — this brief is DRAFTED, NOT DISPATCHED. Dispatch is gated on: (1) the owner's release of the adoption queue, AND (2) D1's verification landing (the mob's 2/3 ordering: cc4's final acceptance follows D1 so the compiler revision it pins is the final one; cc4 PREPARATION — the pinned-digest work — may proceed in parallel with D1 if the orchestrator splits it that way at dispatch). When released, fill the header and dispatch per the routing rules then in force.\\n\\n**DISPATCH GATE — do not run this brief until the orchestrator fills the header above.**\\n\\n## Where you work\\n\\nWorktree: created at dispatch time from then-current `origin/master`, branch `cc4-fourhost-equality`. Work ONLY there. TDD: red first for every acceptance item. Commit NOTHING — the orchestrator commits after review.\\n\\n## POST-CC3 / PORT / REFACTOR AMENDMENT (2026-11-13 — supersedes stale context below)\\n\\nThree landings since this brief was drafted; your pinned-digest cohort and budget record measure THIS master:\\n\\n1. **cc3 landed** (`2c80a421`) — the callsite battery on master is 44+ deftests (the equality-gate upgrade base is `equality-gate-test` at ~:115 plus the r7-r11 retention-state families). Pin digests against THIS battery's output.\\n2. **The port landed** (`309fe842` + kit `ba3cc407` + cljd fix `a3f7ab8d`) — yang.clojure's exception lowering is the continuation encoding (`finally` expressible, one-catch pinned; the outcome machinery retired, net −418 lines). Your pinned cohort's expectations must be recorded from POST-port compilation; per the attribution rule above, any budget shift vs the pre-port measurement attributes to the port's Phase 2 (`d60038ef`).\\n3. **The shell refactor landed** (`c62266ad..6445f37a`): `yin.shell.*` namespaces exist; `repl-query-link-forwarding-test` reads `yin.shell.query` on master (its `:cljd` gate from `4d0d3e70` preserved through the merge). Your J2-lane work (item 2) and the battery's cljd gates reconcile against THIS layout.\\n4. **Jolt lane**: `pair.cljc` (+675 lines) landed in the linker directory from the same refactor — the J2 manifest check (item 2) runs against that tree; the jolt seat's exclusions were relayed as unchanged.\\n\\n## Goal and authority\\n\\ncc4 closes the Clojure frontend's own adoption acceptance: prove that the same Clojure source, compiled on every host, yields **byte-identical C1 side tables and identical occurrence keys**, and record the measured budgets. Authorities:\\n- `collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md` §5.1–5.3 (the mandatory host sets, the cross-host equality without collapsing admissions, the frontend work package), §6 (measurement and budgets).\\n- `collab/yang-clojure/1794344088000-orchestrator-cc3-d1-mob-reconciliation.md` — the mob's Q3 ruling (cc4-final after D1) and the equal-gate-is-per-frontend rule.\\n- `collab/yang-clojure/1794505595000-to-steward-cc3-merged-port-phase-0-released.md` + the landed cc3 chain (`git log` on master from `2c80a421`) — what exists to test against.\\n- The landed battery: `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` (44+ deftests; `equality-gate-test` at :115 is today's single-host self-consistency — cc4 upgrades it to cross-host equality).\\n\\n## The work items (each = acceptance criterion)\\n\\n1. **Pinned cross-host expectations.** Extend `equality-gate-test` (or add a sibling deftest) to assert, for the pinned portable cohort (design §5.2: same source, same grammar/options, same supplied admission coordinates; include floats, metadata, generated temporaries, duplicate trees, macro-generated calls, and the wrapper/prelude surfaces): the canonical root address, the full sorted C1 `[origin root-address path]` vector, and the published `clj`/`yang.call` side-table addresses are IDENTICAL to recorded values — recorded once on the dispatch host, then proven identical on every other host. The cohort must also include the negative fixture (design §5.2: identical text admitted twice with distinct supplied tokens → distinct origins — cross-host equality is replay equality, never content identity).\\n2. **Four-host execution.** Run the strengthened battery on: JVM (the dispatch host), Node (`bb test:cljs` / shadow), Dart (`bb test:cljd` / the cljd aggregator — respecting the existing cljd gates in the file, e.g. `#?(:cljd nil ...)` regions stay gated), and Jolt (`src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` — add the callsite namespace to the J2 lane if absent, per the lane's manifest rules; coordinate with the jolt seat only if the lane's exclusions need a change). Each host's result recorded in findings with exact commands and counts. Where a host cannot run a region (documented cljd `with-redefs` gates), the recorded refusal is the acceptance — gates stay honest, no silent skips.\\n3. **Budget record — MEASURE BOTH (steward coordination 1794484000000, sol-consult-endorsed).** Per design §6.1–6.3 and the cc3 v2-declaration precedent (`1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md` — read it for the format): measure and record, for the pinned corpus on each host, the static side-artifact bytes (C1 rows + provenance relation), the retained-memory and peak-heap figures with the named method and comparability limits, pipeline elapsed times, and the max-based pass/fail verdicts against declared finite ceilings. Declare the ceilings BEFORE measuring (declare from the cc3 v2 baselines + headroom; a measured exceedance is recorded as a failed bound, never a silently raised ceiling). Separate configurations: B (trace disabled) vs S (static annotation) per design §6.2 — S−B is the overhead record.\\n   **Attribution (binding at dispatch):** cc4 measures the POST-port lowering (the encoding all four frontends will run — the port merges before cc4 lands). If any budget shifts vs a pre-port measurement, attribute the shift to the port's Phase 2 (`d60038ef`), not a cc4 regression. Measure BOTH: pre-port baseline = the master commit preceding the port's merge; post = the port branch/merged master. The port's Phase 3 depth harness (on its branch) exists for exactly this comparison.\\n4. **The acceptance bundle.** Assemble per design §5.3's Clojure brief: the artifact checklist, host matrix results, the equality report, the budget tables, legacy-load behavior (unannotated artifacts still load), and the refusal inventory. This bundle is what D1's verifier and future consumers cite.\\n\\n## Bounded file ownership\\n\\nMAY edit: `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`, `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` (lane manifest only), new fixture files under `test/resources/yang/clojure/` if the cohort needs them, and NEW files for the budget record under `test/yang/latte_oracle/` or `collab/` (propose in findings).\\nMUST NOT: any `src/cljc` compiler file (cc4 is a test/acceptance round — if a host divergence is found, STOP and report it as a defect with the diverging artifacts; fixing it is a new round), `slice9_site_tables.edn`, the forbidden set from cc3 (macro.cljc, semantic.cljc, ast_walker.cljc, yang/clojure.cljc, core/prelude.cljc, dht.cljc).\\n\\n## Invariants\\n\\nThe pinned cohort's expectations are recorded data (digests), not recomputed per host at test time — the test compares each host's output to the SAME recorded values. A host that cannot run a region records the refusal; nothing is silently skipped. Origins never minted. No canonical change.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nJVM/Node/Dart battery runs per the build-n-test gate ladder (G1 laptop where allowed; the four-host matrix is inherently shiva/jupiter work — coordinate hosts per the lane-overlap rules; one Dart lane a