\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"model\\\":\\\"glm-5.3\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"thinking\\\",\\\"thinking\\\":\\\"`assoc` and `conj` are pure VM primitives. `identity`, `inc`, `dec`, `count`, `data/count` — `data/count` comes from the data module (`data/register-data-module`). `identity`/`inc`/`dec` are NOT in vm/primitives. So for runtime tests, use only primitives in the registry: `+ - * / = < > not first rest conj assoc get vec` + data module fns (data/count, data/content=, ...). Or pass an :env with host fns? `compile-and-run` accepts env: `(compile-and-run form {'x 100})` — env maps variables to values. Variables resolve from env — I could bind `inc`? No — variable lookup happens... Let me check how the walker resolves `{:type :variable :name 'inc}` — via env or primitives. If env supplies it, `(compile-and-run '((fn [x] x) 1))`... simpler to use primitives directly: use `(+ x 1)` and `(- x 1)` as dynamic key expressions (both applications, different content). For colliding keys: `{(+ 1 1) :a (+ 2 0) :b}` — both evaluate to 2, different code. Good, and both key exprs are applications of `+`.\\\\n\\\\nFor the trace/effect-order tests (family 5): \\\\\\\"Record an observable trace using the existing test harness's explicit effects/streams: key-before-value, canonical pair/element order, no duplication, and no later event after an operand failure/continuation transfer.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nObservable trace — how do tests record evaluation order? Options: use effectful primitives... `vm/primitives` has no effectful user-callable trace primitive except require/try-require. But `clojure_test` base-vm-opts registers stream module — `(dao.stream.apply/call :op/echo ...)`. Hmm. Alternatively bind host functions in the env: does create-vm's :env supply variable bindings as functions? In `compile-and-run`, env maps var names to values. If I bind `probe` to a host function that appends to an atom, then `(probe 1)` compiles as application of variable `probe` → looks up env → host function → calls it. Does the walker/semantic/stack/register VM support calling host functions from env? The values module presumably wraps host fns. Let me check how env values that are functions get applied — search for tests calling env-supplied functions.\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"c1eb1a8dcac14dd2bed1e63c\\\"}],\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"output_tokens\\\":0},\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"09bd2876-81f8-4e67-affe-ac211a92f4e2\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-18T16:22:25.605Z\\\",\\\"thinking_duration_ms\\\":8266,\\\"thinking_display\\\":\\\"updates\\\"}\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795018441000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.stdout.log:21236:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"call_e98ffb13593f4c13beb939fb\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"23:(def ^:private base-vm-opts\\\\n27:(defn compile-and-run\\\\n39:(deftest reader-metadata-becomes-occurrence-side-tables\\\\n55:(deftest indexing-reader-injects-nested-source-positions\\\\n71:(defn compile-program-and-run\\\\n83:(deftest test-compile-literals\\\\n107:(deftest test-set-literal-round-trips\\\\n114:(deftest test-set-literal-row-lane\\\\n132:(deftest test-set-in-application-position\\\\n139:(deftest test-compile-variables\\\\n145:(deftest test-compile-lambda\\\\n159:(deftest test-compile-application\\\\n173:(deftest test-compile-dao-stream-apply-call\\\\n182:(deftest test-compile-if\\\\n200:(deftest test-dynamic-collection-literals\\\\n231:(deftest test-compile-let\\\\n251:(deftest test-compile-do\\\\n266:(deftest test-compile-quote\\\\n272:(deftest test-end-to-end-compilation-and-execution\\\\n310:(deftest test-compile-errors\\\\n320:(deftest test-compile-stream-make\\\\n334:(deftest test-compile-stream