ce is multi-line; same forms. ✓\\\\n\\\\n```clojure\\\\n(def ^:private arity-map-key-order\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The ruled pair order of the named arity map: key roots 1e0366… (:yin.k/fn),\\\\n   81b62c… (:yin.vm.data/reason), 8930bf… (:yin.k/argc) — pinned by the ruling\\\\n   from the unchanged child rows of both hosts' pre-fix evidence.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [:yin.k/fn :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc])\\\\n\\\\n(def ^:private named-arity-operand-roots\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Recorded on the JVM; the child addresses are compiler-revision-stable\\\\n   content addresses (each child compiled identically before and after the\\\\n   ordering fix).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [:segment/blake3-201f235c…  seed {}\\\\n   :segment/blake3-1e03667e…  :yin.k/fn\\\\n   :segment/blake3-3156a070…  'replay\\\\n   :segment/blake3-81b62c1e…  :yin.vm.data/reason\\\\n   :segment/blake3-1db5dbd0…  :arity\\\\n   :segment/blake3-8930bf5e…  :yin.k/argc\\\\n   :segment/blake3-e60543d2…]) ; (data/count dsg__av)\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFinder for arity constructors:\\\\n\\\\n```clojure\\\\n(defn- arity-map-constructors\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The constructed maps naming an arity error: key :yin.k/fn (named) or\\\\n   :yin.k/kind (anonymous) among the operand literals.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [ast]\\\\n  (into [] (filter (fn [c] (some (fn [o] (and (= :literal (:type o))\\\\n                                              (contains? #{:yin.k/fn :yin.k/kind} (:value o))))\\\\n                                 (:operands c))))\\\\n        (collection-applications ast)))\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\ndeftest `arity-map-canonical-order-test`:\\\\n- for BOTH `(yang/compile-program cohort-forms true yang/unit-opts)` and `(yang/lower-unit cohort-forms)`:\\\\n  - constructors exist; named ones (:yin.k/fn) — for lower-unit there are TWO (replay + identity from library); assert for each:\\\\n    - key-literal vector = [:yin.k/fn :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc]\\\\n    - operand-roots = named-arity-operand-roots\\\\n    - pair-keys sorted (oracle)\\\\n    - seed first, even operand count\\\\n    - the argc value is a (data/count dsg__av) application; fn value literal 'replay or 'identity\\\\n- anonymous: compile `[(with-meta '(fn [x] x) nil)]` and `[(with-meta '(fn [x] x) {:line 7 :column 2})]` under unit-opts:\\\\n  - key order [:yin.k/kind :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc] (nil-meta: 3 pairs)\\\\n  - with-source: [:yin.k/kind :yin.k/source :yin.vm.data/reason :yin.k/argc], :yin.k/source value {:line 7 :column 2}\\\\n  - operand roots recorded vectors for both\\\\n- payload values at runtime (outcome lane): local outcome-opts/modules; run `[(defn arity2 [x] x) (arity2 1 2)]` → [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/fn 'arity2 :yin.vm.data/reason :arity :yin.k/argc 2}] — value = map equality (order-free). Also anonymous → {:yin.k/kind :anonymous :yin.k/argc 1 ...}.\\\\n\\\\nHmm wait — with :outcomes, `defn arity2` compiles to av-fn; call with 2 args → argc=2. The error payload — let me confirm the runtime shape by trying. I'll write it and adjust after running.\\\\n\\\\n**§2 Family 2 — map permutations.**\\\\n\\\\nCorpus definition. Represent each case as `[label entries]` where entries is a vector of `[key-form value-form]`.\\\\n\\\\n```clojure\\\\n(def ^:private map-corpus\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Recorded corpus (ruling test 2): distinct source-entry pairs. Every case\\\\n   holds at least one dynamic expression.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [[:constant-keys-dynamic-values [[:a '(+ n 0)] [:b '(+ n 1)]]]\\\\n   [:dynamic-keys [['(first xs) :v1] ['(first (rest xs)) :v2]]]\\\\n   [:heterogeneous-scalar-keys\\\\n    [[:kw '(+ n 0)] [\\\\\\\"str\\\\\\\" 1] [3 1.5] ['sym '(rest xs)] [(quote true) 0] [nil 2]]]\\\\n```\\\\nHmm wait — entry `[nil 2]`: constant; `[\\\\\\\"str\\\\\\\" 1]` constant... the MAP needs ≥1 dynamic to reach the emitter — `:kw '(+ n 0)` provides it. Heterogeneous keys: keyword, string, long, double, symbol, boolean, nil, quoted collection, quoted collection with metadata. Values mostly constants.\\\\n\\\\nQuoted collection key: `'(quote [1 2])`; with-meta: build form at