rm (perms (count entries))\\\\n                           :let [pe (permute-entries entries perm)]\\\\n                           rep [array-map-fn hash-map-fn]\\\\n                           :let [form (build rep pe)]]\\\\n                       form)\\\\n            snaps (mapv #(snapshot-of (yang/compile %)) variants)]\\\\n        (is (apply = snaps) ...)\\\\n        (doseq [ast ...] (is (ctor-pairs-sorted? ast)))))))\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nsnapshot-of: compile → encoder/project → tree+rows → digests (root, keys, c1, provenance). \\\\n\\\\nPermutation count control: sizes 0-4 all perms; 8/9/16/32 recorded set (forward, reverse, rot1..3, shuffle ×2 seeds) × 2 reps. Map building cost: compile 32-entry map with permutations — each compile projects 64 children... fine.\\\\n\\\\n**§3 Family 3 — sets.** Mirror with set corpus:\\\\n```clojure\\\\n[:dynamic-elements ['(+ n 0) '(first xs) ...]]\\\\n[:nested-dynamic-sets ['#{(+ n 1)} '(second xs) 2]]\\\\n[:colliding-value-expressions ['(mod n 2)?? — no mod primitive needed for COMPILE-only] ...]\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\\\\"Include nested dynamic sets and different expressions evaluating to the same value\\\\\\\" — compile-time: two different exprs `(first xs)` and `'(first xs)`... same-value needs runtime — execution covers it; corpus includes the forms. Representations: `(set (vec elems-in-perm-order))` — hmm `(set v)` dedups by value — the ELEMENTS are FORMS (distinct lists), so set keeps all. Also `apply hash-set`. For array-set? No array-set in clojure — sorted-set? \\\\\\\"available ordinary\\\\\\\" representations — literal #{} from file, `(set ...)`, `(apply hash-set ...)`. On hosts, `hash-set` iteration differs (JVM hash vs Dart hash) → post-fix invariant anyway.\\\\n\\\\nElement sort key: single root. Assert sortedness oracle + snapshot invariance across permutations/representations.\\\\n\\\\n**§4 Family 4 — oracle:**\\\\n```clojure\\\\n(deftest order-pairing-multiplicity-oracle-test ...)\\\\n```\\\\n- for each corpus map compile: seed-first, even count, pair-keys sorted, pairs match independently compiled entries (multiset), metadata invariance (with-meta variants), tie preservation (identical pairs kept: `{x :v x :v}` — construct with duplicate keys? A HOST MAP CANNOT HAVE DUPLICATE KEYS — `{x :v x :v}` evaluates to {x :v} — one entry! Duplicate ENTRIES can't exist in a host map. Hmm! \\\\\\\"add distinct forms compiling to an identical entire pair/element to exercise ties without occurrence loss\\\\\\\" — for MAPS: distinct forms that compile to the same PAIR — e.g. key `(quote x)` vs `x`? compile differently. Key `x` value `(+ n 0)` vs key `x` value... identical pair means identical key code AND value code: two DIFFERENT source forms compiling to identical code: e.g. key `x` (symbol) vs key form `(quote x)`? no that's quoted data. How about values: `(+ n 0)` and... two syntactically different forms with same compile: `(+ n 0)` vs `(+ n 0)` with different metadata! `(with-meta '(+ n 0) {:line 5})` vs plain — same projected content (meta dropped), different source. That's the tie: two entries whose compiled pairs are content-identical → equal sort keys → both occurrences preserved (4 operands for 2 entries). For SETS: `#{(+ n 0) (+ n 0)}` — host set DEDUPES identical forms by value! Two IDENTICAL forms are = → one element. So ties in sets need distinct-but-equivalent forms: `#{(with-meta '(+ n 0) {:line 9}) (+ n 0)}` — distinct host values (different meta) → set keeps 2 → both compile to identical code → tie. ✓ Same trick for maps.\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Changing only source-position or variable-node metadata MUST NOT change code order/root\\\\\\\": compile plain vs with-meta-positions → same root; and the operand-root vectors equal.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Preserve semantic metadata in literal payloads\\\\\\\": quoted-with-meta key vs without → roots DIFFER (metadata is content) — both orders still sorted.\\\\n\\\\n**§5 Family 5 — execution** (as planned).\\\\n\\\\n**§6 Family 6 — entry points + macro.**\\\\n\\\\n**§7 Family 7 — legacy + tokens.**\\\\n\\\\nAlso needed: `expand-like-the-repl` local copy (macro seed/expand) — requires yin.vm.macro ✓.\\\\n\\\\nLength concern: this namespace will be ~600-800 lines. That's expected for this codebase's test style.\\\\n\\\\nOne more mechanical detail — `vm/ast->semantic-bytecode` returns `{:root ...}` where root is a keyword `:segment/blake3-…`. `jing/canonical-compare` over VECTORS of these keywords ✓.\\\\n\\\\nNow about `(sort jing/canonical-compare coll)` — sorting EDN tuples containing keywords/vectors ✓ (cohort does this).\\\\n\\\\nWriting now. I'll be careful with quote levels. Also remember: cljd lane — avoid `(quote ...)` inside #{} reader? Sets as data fine. Avoid regex, avoid `->>` with lazy? fine.\\\\n\\\\nOne CLJS gotcha: `(apply array-map flat)` where flat is seq — OK. `(apply hash-map flat)` OK. On cljd — array-map/hash-map exist ✓.\\\\n\\\\nDart: `keyword` fn `(keyword (str \\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\" i))` ✓.\\\\n\\\\nAnother gotcha: on CLJS, `=` of my snapshot maps with keyword keys ✓.\\\\n\\\\nLet me also decide the snapshot to include `:applications` count (cohort has it) — count of marked occurrences — permutation-invariant post-fix ✓.\\\\n\\\\nFor the stack/register image opts — cohort used `{:segment-address :cc4/stack :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)}` — mirror with :fixorder/stack.\\\\n\\\\n`linearize/project-rows tree nil rows` — signature (tree, ?, rows) with nil for what? In cohort: `(linearize/project-rows tree nil rows)`. Check signature quickly.\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"33b0b6f675cd4fff8b3175a3\\\"}],\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"output_tokens\\\":0},\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"6ddd8e9c-e17a-4869-8b3e-6766d0b5a374\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-18T16:38:24.983Z\\\",\\\"thinking_duration_ms\\\":55232,\\\"thinking_display\\\":\\\"updates\\\"}\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795018441000-engineer-fix-constructed-collection-order-r1.glm-5.3.stdout.log:46082:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_20261119003831680aa2b1025246a7\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"model\\\":\\\"glm-5.3\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"call_730840fc1b9e4241b395d4ea\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nsrc = r'''(ns yang.clojure-collection-order-test\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Constructed collections v1 (architect ruling 1795017757000, RULING 1-4):\\\\n   the canonical operand ordering of dynamically constructed map and set\\\\n   literals at yang.clojure's collection emitter, the evaluation semantics\\\\n   that ordering makes executable, and the manifest/legacy boundaries of the\\\\n   c1-2 revision.\\\\n\\\\n   Every order expectation here comes from builders independent of the\\\\n   emitter's own sort: children project through\\\\n   yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode and order through dao.jing/canonical-compare\\\\n   (RFC 8949 canonical bytes, unsigned bytewise, proper prefix first), the\\\\n   same comparator the ruling names — never through the helper under test.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\\\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\\\\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\\\\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\\\n            [dao.stream.base64 :as base64]\\\\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\\\\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\\\\n            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\\\\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\\\\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\\\\n            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\\\\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\\\\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\\\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\\\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\\\\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\\\\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\\\\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\n;; Independent oracle builders (RULING 1's comparator, not the emitter's sort)\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\n\\\\n(defn- collection-applications\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Every constructor application of compiled `ast` — an assoc over the {}\\\\n   seed or a conj over the []/#{} seed — outermost walk order. A program\\\\n   under test contains either only emitter output or only the explicit\\\\n   constructor calls a control names, never both.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [ast]\\\\n  (let [acc (atom [])]\\\\n    (walk/postwalk\\\\n      (fn [n]\\\\n        (when (and (map? n)\\\\n                   (= :application (:type n))\\\\n                   (= :variable (get-in n [:operator :type]))\\\\n                   (= :literal (get-in n [:operands 0 :type]))\\\\n                   (contains? #{['assoc {}] ['conj []] ['conj #{}]}\\\\n                              [(get-in n [:operator :name])\\\\n                               (get-in n [:operands 0 :value])]))\\\\n          (swap! acc conj n))\\\\n        n)\\\\n      ast)\\\\n    @acc))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- map-constructors [ast]\\\\n  (into [] (filter #(= (quote assoc) (get-in % [:operator :name])))\\\\n        (collection-applications ast)))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- child-roots\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of each operand of `node`,\\\\n   projected independently of the emitter.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [node]\\\\n  (mapv (fn [o] (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode o))) (:operands node)))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- seed-root\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The recorded root of the empty-map seed literal (a content address:\\\\n   stable across hosts and compiler revisions).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  []\\\\n  :segment/blake3-201f235cbac998f43954454e9df0eb633717e79de535776f3f51e198a3759b10)\\\\n\\\\n(defn- pair-keys\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The RULING 1 sort keys of a map constructor's pairs: `[key-root\\\\n   value-root]` per source pair, in emitted order.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [node]\\\\n  (mapv vec (partition 2 (rest (child-roots node)))))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- element-keys\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The RULING 1 sort keys of a set constructor's elements (one root each),\\\\n   in emitted order.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [node]\\\\n  (mapv vector (rest (child-roots node))))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- ascending?\\\\n  \\\\\\\"True when `ks` is strictly sorted by jing/canonical-compare; equal keys\\\\n   are equal executable content and a tie is legal anywhere.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [ks]\\\\n  (every? (fn [[a b]] (neg? (jing/canonical-compare a b)))\\\\n          (partition 2 1 ks)))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- key-literals\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Every second operand's literal value (the map keys), for reading an\\\\n   emitted order against recorded expectations.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [node]\\\\n  (mapv (fn [o] (when (= :literal (:type o)) (:value o)))\\\\n        (take-nth 2 (rest (:operands node)))))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- project-batch\\\\n  \\\\\\\"One compiled ast through the production encoder envelope under `token`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ([ast] (project-batch ast \\\\\\\"order-a\\\\\\\"))\\\\n  ([ast token]\\\\n   (let [p (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope :cc4/replay token [ast]))]\\\\n     {:tree (first (:yin/batch p))\\\\n      :rows (:yin/frontend-metadata p)})))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- digest-snapshot\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The equality snapshot of one projected batch: root, the canonical-sorted\\\\n   C1 marker relation, the sorted occurrence-key vector and all three\\\\n   instruction formats' call-provenance — the cohort's model, nothing\\\\n   normalized away.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [{:keys [tree rows]}]\\\\n  (let [c1 (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\\\\n                      (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)) rows)))\\\\n        keys (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\\\\n                        (into [] (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\\\\n                                       (map #(vec (take 3 %)))) rows)))\\\\n        sem (linearize/project-rows tree nil rows)\\\\n        stack (derive/stack-image (:vector sem)\\\\n                                  {:segment-address :order/stack\\\\n                                   :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})\\\\n        register (derive/register-image (:vector sem)\\\\n                                        {:segment-address :order/register\\\\n                                         :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})]\\\\n    {:root (:root tree)\\\\n     :applications (count keys)\\\\n     :keys-digest (jing/content-hash keys)\\\\n     :c1-digest (jing/content-hash c1)\\\\n     :instruction-provenance-digest\\\\n     (jing/content-hash [(:call-provenance sem)\\\\n                         (:call-provenance stack)\\\\n                         (:call-provenance register)])}))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- compile-snapshot\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Compile `form`, project it, digest it.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [form]\\\\n  (digest-snapshot (project-batch (yang/compile form))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\n;; Execution routes (RULING 2/3: walker, semantic, stack, register)\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\n\\\\n(def ^:private registry\\\\n  (-> (module/empty-registry)\\\\n      module/register-cell-module\\\\n      data/register-data-module))\\\\n\\\\n(def ^:private base-opts\\\\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream\\\\n   :capability-secret tu/secret\\\\n   :primitives vm/primitives\\\\n   :modules registry})\\\\n\\\\n(def ^:private load-semantic-ast\\\\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- run-on\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Run compiled `ast` on every execution route, returning lane -> value.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ([ast] (run-on ast {}))\\\\n  ([ast env]\\\\n   (let [opts (assoc base-opts :env env)\\\\n         runners\\\\n         {:ast-walker (fn [] (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast))\\\\n          :semantic (fn [] (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\\\\n                                                      (vm/ast->datoms ast))))\\\\n          :stack (fn [] (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\\\\n                                  (:image (derive/stack-image\\\\n                                            (:vector (linearize/project ast))))\\\\n                                  (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))))\\\\n          :register (fn [] (vm/run (rvm/create-vm\\\\n                                     (derive/register-image\\\\n                                       (:vector (linearize/project ast)))\\\\n                                     (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))}]\\\\n     (into {} (map (fn [[lane run]] [lane (vm/value (run))])) runners))))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- run-form\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Compile and run `form` on every route with `env`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ([form] (run-form form {}))\\\\n  ([form env] (run-on (yang/compile form) env)))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- trace-of\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The observable trace of `form` on every route: each lane's value and the\\\\n   ordered log the env-bound `tap` host function recorded while producing\\\\n   it. `tap` echoes its argument, so the log is the operand evaluation\\\\n   order.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  ([form] (trace-of form {}))\\\\n  ([form env]\\\\n   (let [log (atom [])]\\\\n     (into {}\\\\n           (map (fn [[lane value]] [lane {:value value :log @log}]))\\\\n           (do (reset! log [])\\\\n               (run-form form (assoc env 'tap (fn [x] (swap! log conj x) x))))))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\n;; Deterministic permutation machinery (RULING 3: recorded data, no host rand)\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\n\\\\n(defn- all-permutations\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Every ordering of (range n), the plain recursive enumeration.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [n]\\\\n  (if (zero? n)\\\\n    [[]]\\\\n    (mapcat (fn [i]\\\\n              (map #(into [i] %)\\\\n                   (all-permutations (remove #{i} (range n)))))\\\\n            (range n))))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- rotate\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The kth rotation of `v`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [k v]\\\\n  (let [k (mod k (count v))]\\\\n    (into (subvec v k) (subvec v 0 k))))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- lcg\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The recorded-seed Lehmer generator: x' = 48271*x mod (2^31-2). Every\\\\n   product stays below 2^53, so every host's double arithmetic computes the\\\\n   identical sequence (a JVM long-math generator would not be portable).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [seed n]\\\\n  (into [] (map (fn [_ x] (mod (* 48271 x) 2147483646)) (repeat n 0))\\\\n        (rest (iterate (fn [x] (mod (* 48271 x) 2147483646)) seed))))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- lcg-shuffle\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Fisher-Yates over `v` driven by the recorded-seed Lehmer generator.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [seed v]\\\\n  (let [n (count v)]\\\\n    (if (< n 2)\\\\n      (vec v)\\\\n      (let [states (lcg seed (dec n))]\\\\n        (loop [i (dec n), s states, acc (vec v)]\\\\n          (if (zero? i)\\\\n            acc\\\\n            (let [j (mod (first s) (inc i))]\\\\n              (recur (dec i) (rest s)\\\\n                     (assoc acc i (nth acc j) j (nth acc i))))))))))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- recorded-permutations\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The recorded permutation set for sizes beyond the full enumeration:\\\\n   forward, reverse, four rotations and two seeded shuffles.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [n seed]\\\\n  (into []\\\\n        (map vec)\\\\n        [(range n)\\\\n         (reverse (range n))\\\\n         (rotate 1 (vec (range n)))\\\\n         (rotate 2 (vec (range n)))\\\\n         (rotate 3 (vec (range n)))\\\\n         (lcg-shuffle seed (vec (range n)))\\\\n         (lcg-shuffle (inc seed) (vec (range n)))]))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- permute\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The entries of `v` reordered by index vector `p`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [v p]\\\\n  (into [] (map v) p))\\\\n\\\\n(defn- build-map\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The logical entries as a host map value in `order`, through the array-map\\\\n   or hash-map representation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [rep entries]\\\\n  (let [flat (into [] (mapcat identity) entries)]\\\\n    (if (= :array-map rep)\\\\n      (apply array-map flat)\\\\n      (apply hash-map flat))))\\\\n'''\\\\nPath(\\\\\\\"test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\\\\\\\").write_text(src)\\\\nprint(\\\\\\\"part1 written\\\\\\\", len(src))\\\\nPYEOF\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Write test namespace part 1 (helpers)\\\"}}],\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"output_tokens\\\":0},\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"1e1c5d85-861b-47a7-9f28-18c211a6a264\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-18T16:39:06.273Z\\\",\\\"wire_tool_inputs\\\":{\\\"call_730840fc1b9e4241b395d4ea\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nsrc = r'''(ns yang.clojure-collection-order-test\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Constructed collections v1 (architect ruling 1795017757000, RULING 1-4):\\\\n   the canonical operand ordering of dynamically constructed map and set\\\\n   literals at yang.clojure's collection emitter, the evaluation semantics\\\\n   that ordering makes executable, and the manifest/legacy boundaries of the\\\\n   c1-2 revision.\\\\n\\\\n   Every order expectation here comes from builders independent of the\\\\n   emitter's own sort: children project through\\\\n   yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode and order through dao.jing/canonical-compare\\\\n   (RFC 8949 canonical bytes, unsigned bytewise, proper prefix first), the\\\\n   same comparator the ruling names — never through the helper under test.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\\\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\\\\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\\\\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\\\n            [dao.stream.base64 :as base64]\\\\n      