{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"The code confirms a runtime correctness defect: losing float kind changes `data/equiv`, key admission, and arithmetic dispatch. `yang.clojure/read-forms` uses upstream `cljs.tools.reader`, and the public forms API can receive already-collapsed values. The ruling needs to distinguish preserving kind while reading source from the caller’s obligation when supplying Data directly."}}
