{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md\nsed -n '1,115p' src/cljc/yang/clojure/core_impl.cljc\nsed -n '1,95p' src/cljc/yang/clojure/core_module.cljc\nrg -n 'float64|equiv|admit-key|content=' test/yin/vm/data_test.cljc test/yin/vm/float_test.cljc | head -80\nrg --files /Users/sto/.m2/repository/org/clojure/tools.reader /Users/sto/.m2/repository/org/clojure/clojurescript .cpcache .shadow-cljs | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \"name\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \"Remote test servers\" below for\n# which lanes may overlap.\n#\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n# When a test fails, reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the failing test\n# (`clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>`, Node `--test=<ns>`, Dart `--only <ns>`) --\n# never the whole suite (owner ruling 2026-11-01; see Gate Ladder G0).\n# Individual tests run fine on the laptop; suite-scale runs (G1 subsystem sets,\n# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\n# the suite has outgrown the laptop (owner ruling 2026-11-04).\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` runs once daily on the remote hosts (04:00 VN);\n# a MERGE needs only the affected tests (bb test:changed) -- owner ruling 2026-11-01;\n# for a fix branch, the previously-failing tests green IS the merge bar\n# (owner ruling 2026-11-07; see Gate Ladder G0).\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\n# overlap lanes, see \"Remote test servers\" below).\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\n```\n\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\nmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\ntests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\nA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\nneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\n`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\ntypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\nland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\nchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\nantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\nas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\ndao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\n(ns yang.clojure.core-impl\n  \"Stateless guest operations for the portable Clojure standard library.\"\n  (:require [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n            [yang.core.prelude-admission :as admission]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]\n            [yang.rt.int :as int-rt]))\n\n\n(def module-name 'clojure.core.impl)\n\n\n(def ^:private helpers\n  '[[impl-cell-ref?\n     (fn [x]\n       (if (data/map? x)\n         (if (= (get x :type) :cell-ref) (cell/authentic? x) false)\n         false))]\n    [impl-map? (fn [x] (if (data/map? x) (not (impl-cell-ref? x)) false))]\n    [impl-coll? (fn [x] (if (data/map? x) (not (impl-cell-ref? x)) (kind/coll? x)))]\n    [impl-sequential?\n     (fn [x] (if (data/map? x) false (if (kind/coll? x) (not (kind/set? x)) false)))]\n    [impl-seq? (fn [x] (if (impl-sequential? x) (not (data/vector? x)) false))]\n    [impl-error\n     (fn [message data]\n       (clj/raise (assoc {} :yin.k/message message :yin.k/data data)))]\n    [impl-int-result\n     (fn [value] (yrt.int/check-limit (clj/rt-ctx) value))]\n    [impl-lookup-view\n     (fn [x]\n       (if (if (data/map? x) (= :cell-ref (get x :type)) false)\n         (clj/condition-view x)\n         x))]\n    [impl-get-default\n     (fn [coll k default]\n       (clj/prim-get-default coll (if (data/vector? coll) k (clj/collection-key k)) default))]\n    [impl-assoc-one\n     (fn [coll k v]\n       (assoc coll (if (data/vector? coll) k (clj/collection-key k)) v))]\n    [impl-get-path\n     (fn [coll path i n default]\n       (if (< i n)\n         (let [k (data/nth path i)\n               indexed? (data/vector? coll)\n               map? (impl-map? coll)\n               key (if map? (clj/collection-key k) k)]\n           (if (if indexed? (data/contains? coll key)\n                 (if map? (data/contains? coll key) false))\n             (impl-get-path (clj/prim-get coll key) path (+ i 1) n default)\n             default))\n         coll))]\n    [impl-assoc-path\n     (fn [coll path i n value]\n       (let [k (if (< i n) (data/nth path i) nil)]\n         (impl-assoc-one coll k\n           (if (< (+ i 1) n)\n             (impl-assoc-path (impl-get-default coll k nil) path (+ i 1) n value)\n             value))))]\n    [impl-assoc-more\n     (fn [coll args i n]\n       (if (< i n)\n         (impl-assoc-more (impl-assoc-one coll (data/nth args i) (data/nth args (+ i 1)))\n                          args (+ i 2) n)\n         coll))]\n    [impl-vec\n     (fn [xs]\n       (if (data/vector? xs) xs\n         (if (data/map? xs)\n           (if (impl-cell-ref? xs)\n             (impl-error \"Cannot traverse a cell reference\" {})\n             (data/canonical-entries xs))\n           (if (kind/set? xs) (data/canonical-entries xs) (vec xs)))))]\n    [impl-first\n     (fn [xs]\n       (if (if (data/map? xs) true (kind/set? xs))\n         (first (impl-vec xs))\n         (first xs)))]\n    [impl-prepend-reversed\n     (fn [xs i acc]\n       (if (< i 0)\n         acc\n         (impl-prepend-reversed xs (- i 1) (conj acc (data/nth xs i)))))]\n    [impl-list-from (fn [xs] (impl-prepend-reversed xs (- (data/count xs) 1) (quote ())))]\n    [impl-rest (fn [xs] (impl-list-from (rest (impl-vec xs))))]\n    [impl-reverse-at\n     (fn [xs i n acc]\n       (if (< i n)\n         (impl-reverse-at xs (+ i 1) n (conj acc (data/nth xs i)))\n         acc))]\n    [impl-reverse\n     (fn [xs] (let [v (impl-vec xs)] (impl-reverse-at v 0 (data/count v) (quote ()))))]\n    [impl-seq\n     (fn [xs]\n       (if (nil? xs) nil\n         (if (impl-coll? xs)\n           (if (empty? xs) nil (if (impl-seq? xs) xs (impl-list-from (impl-vec xs))))\n           (impl-error \"seq of a non-collection is not supported\" (assoc {} :value xs)))))]\n    [impl-nth (fn [xs i] (if (nil? xs) nil (data/nth (impl-vec xs) i)))]\n    [impl-contains?\n     (fn [xs k] (data/contains? xs (if (data/vector? xs) k (clj/collection-key k))))]\n    [impl-into-at\n     (fn [to xs i n]\n       (if (< i n)\n         (impl-into-at (impl-conj-one to (data/nth xs i)) xs (+ i 1) n)\n         to))]\n    [impl-into\n     (fn [to from] (let [xs (impl-vec from)] (impl-into-at to xs 0 (data/count xs))))]\n    [impl-conj-one\n     (fn [to x]\n       (if (kind/set? to)\n         (conj to (clj/collection-key x))\n         (if (impl-map? to)\n           (if (impl-map? x)\n(ns yang.clojure.core-module\n  \"Cell-free publication and task-local initialization of the Clojure library.\"\n  (:require [yang.clojure.core-impl :as impl]\n            [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj]\n            [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n            [yang.core.prelude-admission :as admission]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n\n\n(def module-name 'clojure.core)\n\n(def ^:private table-key 'clojure.core.rt/exports)\n(def ^:private uninitialized :clojure.core/uninitialized)\n\n\n(defn accessor-name [name]\n  (symbol (str module-name) (str name)))\n\n\n(defn entry-key [name]\n  (symbol \"clojure.core.rt\" (str name)))\n\n\n(def source-names\n  ;; The Clojure lowerer already emits these predicates as VM primitives.\n  ;; The facade also offers cell accessors for descriptor projections.\n  (disj (set impl/public-names) 'empty? 'nil?))\n\n\n(defn referenced-exports [free-names]\n  (into #{}\n        (keep (fn [sym]\n                (when (= \"clojure.core\" (namespace sym))\n                  (let [name (symbol (name sym))]\n                    (when (contains? source-names name) name)))))\n        free-names))\n\n\n(defn- facade-definitions [names]\n  (let [populate\n        (reduce (fn [table name]\n                  (list 'clj/prim-assoc table (list 'quote name)\n                        (list 'clj/make-source-callable (list 'quote (entry-key name))\n                              {:clj/type :function} (impl/callable-entry name))))\n                {} names)]\n    (into [[table-key uninitialized]\n           ['clojure.core/init!\n            (list 'fn []\n                  (list 'if (list 'data/content= table-key uninitialized)\n                        (core/define table-key populate)\n                        nil))]\n           ['clojure.core/export '(fn [name] (clj/prim-get clojure.core.rt/exports name))]]\n          (map (fn [name]\n                 [(accessor-name name) (list 'fn [] (list 'clojure.core/export (list 'quote name)))]))\n          names)))\n\n\n(def ^:private definitions (facade-definitions impl/public-names))\n\n\n(def module-exports (core/exports (str module-name) definitions))\n\n\n(defn bundled-uast\n  \"Install the same facade over the subset of exports the bundled unit reads.\"\n  [names]\n  (let [names (filterv names impl/public-names)]\n    (u/seq-nodes [(impl/bundled-uast names)\n                  (core/balanced-definitions->uast (facade-definitions names))\n                  (u/app (u/v 'clojure.core/init!))])))\n\n\n(def module-uast\n  (let [nodes (mapv (fn [[name body]] (u/def! name (u/sexp->uast body)))\n                    (core/module-definitions (str module-name) uninitialized [] definitions))\n        [facade accessors] (split-at 3 nodes)\n        requires (mapv u/sexp->uast '[(require 'clj) (require 'clojure.core.impl)])]\n    ;; The table and export reader dominate the accessor bodies. Load the\n    ;; dependencies before installing accessors named after VM primitives.\n    (u/annotate-call-sites (core/wide-app (concat facade requires accessors)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private free-names (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n\n\n(defn module-spec [registry clj-address impl-address]\n  (let [requires {clj/module-name clj-address impl/module-name impl-address}]\n    (admission/module-spec\n      {:module-name module-name :ast module-uast :exports module-exports\n       :requires requires :free-names free-names\n       :skip? #(contains? requires (some-> % namespace symbol))\n       :registry registry :message \"clojure.core reads an undeclared name\"\n       :refusal-ns \"yang.clojure\"})))\ntest/yin/vm/float_test.cljc:10:(defn- box [x] (data/float64 x))\ntest/yin/vm/float_test.cljc:11:(defn- bits [x] (host/float64->bits (data/float-value x)))\ntest/yin/vm/float_test.cljc:21:  (is (false? ((get data/data-module 'equiv) (call 'nan) (call 'nan))))\ntest/yin/vm/float_test.cljc:22:  (is (true? ((get data/data-module 'equiv) (call 'zero) (call 'neg-zero)))))\ntest/yin/vm/data_test.cljc:42:                 (normalize [1 (cbor/float64 2.0)])))))\ntest/yin/vm/data_test.cljc:342:  (testing \"float64 is Jing float64 content, kind kept for an integral\ntest/yin/vm/data_test.cljc:344:    (is (cbor/float64? (call 'float64 1)))\ntest/yin/vm/data_test.cljc:345:    (is (= (jing/segment-key (cbor/float64 1))\ntest/yin/vm/data_test.cljc:346:           (jing/segment-key (call 'float64 1))))\ntest/yin/vm/data_test.cljc:347:   